item.description:
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:justify&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt;Req ID: 28677 &lt;br&gt;Vacancy Type: Temporary &lt;br&gt;Contract Duration: January - April, 2027&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt;Number of Positions: 1  &lt;br&gt;Closing Date: 10/21/2026&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:justify&quot;&gt; &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:justify&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;To be considered for this competition, applicants must be enrolled in a recognized post‑secondary co-op program and be eligible to complete a Work Term during the specified period. Applicants must be legally eligible to work in Canada. Proof of enrolment in a related program must be uploaded when completing the application.&lt;/strong&gt;     &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:justify&quot;&gt; &lt;/p&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;padding:10.0px 0.0px;border:1.0px solid transparent&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:18.0px;word-wrap:break-word&quot;&gt;&lt;H2 style=&quot;font-size:1.0em;margin:0.0px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Job Summary&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/H2&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;The NET Developer Co-op Student will assist with the development, maintenance, and support of web applications and software solutions using .NET technologies. Working alongside the development team, the student will gain hands-on experience with modern web development, cloud technologies, APIs, databases, and DevOps practices while contributing to application enhancements, testing, troubleshooting, and documentation.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;padding:10.0px 0.0px;border:1.0px solid transparent&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:18.0px;word-wrap:break-word&quot;&gt;&lt;H2 style=&quot;font-size:1.0em;margin:0.0px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Duties and Responsibilities&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/H2&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;•    Assist with developing and maintaining web applications using ASP.NET Core MVC / .NET Core. &lt;br&gt;•    Support and maintain legacy .NET Framework MVC applications. &lt;br&gt;•    Build and improve modern user interfaces using Lit Components and modern UI frameworks. &lt;br&gt;•    Assist with developing REST APIs and database-driven applications. &lt;br&gt;•    Gain hands-on experience with AWS services, including ECS and ECR. &lt;br&gt;•    Use Azure DevOps for source control, CI/CD, and development workflows. &lt;br&gt;•    Assist with testing, troubleshooting, documentation, and application improvements. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;padding:10.0px 0.0px;border:1.0px solid transparent&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:18.0px;word-wrap:break-word&quot;&gt;&lt;H2 style=&quot;font-size:1.0em;margin:0.0px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Skills and Qualifications&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/H2&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;•    Currently enrolled in a University or College program related to Computer Science, Software Development, Web Development, Information Technology, or a related field.&lt;br&gt;•    Basic knowledge of C# and .NET / .NET Core. &lt;br&gt;•    Familiarity with ASP.NET MVC and/or .NET Framework MVC. &lt;br&gt;•    Basic knowledge of HTML, CSS (Bootstrap), JavaScript (JQuery) and TypeScript. &lt;br&gt;•    Familiarity with modern UI frameworks (Angular, Vue, React) and Lit Components is an asset. &lt;br&gt;•    Familiarity with AWS (ECS, ECR, S3, SES). &lt;br&gt;•    Familiarity with Azure DevOps and Git. &lt;br&gt;•    Basic understanding of REST APIs and relational databases. &lt;br&gt;•    Strong willingness to learn and work collaboratively in a team. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:left&quot;&gt;Hourly Rate/Salary: 20.64 - 24.53&lt;br&gt;Hours of Work: 35&lt;br&gt;Work Location: Civic Centre&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:red&quot;&gt; &lt;span style=&quot;color:black&quot;&gt;Hybrid Workplace &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;Organization Unit: CPS/Net &amp;amp; Custom Apps&lt;br&gt;Department/Division/Section: CPS/Corporate Services Dept , CPS/IT Division , Enterprise Business Solutions&lt;br&gt;Non-Union/Union: Non Union&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Applicants applying to this posting may be considered for the same position(s) should another vacancy occur within six months from the date of this posting, unless the requirement to repost is expressed differently in a Collective Agreement.&lt;br&gt;If you are selected for an interview and your proposed transfer or promotion results in a real or perceived conflict of interest in relation to the Employment of Relatives Corporate Policy and Procedure, you must notify the Human Resources Representative as soon as possible.&lt;br&gt;If you are selected for an interview you are expected to disclose all current positions held in the City, whether full time or part time.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI (Artificial Intelligence)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The City of Mississauga may use artificial intelligence (AI) technology in sourcing and/or screening candidates for some positions; however, it is not used in selecting final candidates&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Candidates are expected to complete interviews independently to ensure an equitable assessment. The use of AI-generated responses, AI assistants, transcription tools, or third-party coaching technologies during interviews is prohibited, unless supported by an approved accommodation and may result in disqualification from the recruitment process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Accommodations&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;The City of Mississauga is an Equal Opportunity Employer and is committed to removing barriers in our selection process for people with visible and invisible disabilities. In accordance with the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act, 2005 and the Ontario Human Rights Code, the City of Mississauga will provide accommodations throughout the recruitment, selection and/or assessment process to applicants with disabilities.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;If selected to participate in the recruitment, selection and/or assessment process, please complete the following &lt;a href=&quot;https://www7.mississauga.ca/documents/inside/talent/accommodation_request_form.pdf&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener&quot;&gt;Accommodation Request Form&lt;/a&gt; and have it emailed to &lt;a href=&quot;mailto:recruitment.accommodation@mississauga.ca&quot;&gt;recruitment.accommodation@mississauga.ca&lt;/a&gt; citing the Job ID and Job Title. This will inform Human Resources of the nature of any accommodation(s) that you may require in respect of any materials or processes used to ensure your equal participation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0.0px;text-align:left&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equity, Diversity and Inclusion&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;The City of Mississauga is committed to creating a respectful and supportive workplace that fosters a culture of equity, diversity and inclusion which broadly reflects the communities and residents we serve. Throughout the employee life cycle, the City is working to include an EDI lens to attract, retain and support the growth of diverse talent.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Learn more about the City’s commitment to &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.mississauga.ca/our-organization/equity-diversity-and-inclusion/&quot;&gt;Equity, Diversity and Inclusion&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:left&quot;&gt; &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:left&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt; &lt;img src=&quot;https://www7.mississauga.ca/documents/inside/talent/forbes_2026_footer_image.jpg&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; width=&quot;450&quot; height=&quot;101&quot;&gt; &lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:justify;margin:0.0&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt;Req ID: 28678&lt;br&gt;Vacancy Type: Temporary for 2 years with full benefits&lt;br&gt;Number of Positions: 1  &lt;br&gt;Closing Date: 10/23/2026&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;padding:10.0px 0.0px;border:1.0px solid transparent&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:18.0px;word-wrap:break-word&quot;&gt;&lt;H2 style=&quot;font-size:1.0em;margin:0.0px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Job Summary&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/H2&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;As a DevOps Specialist, you will work with technical teams across the organization to implement DevOps strategies and automate applications and infrastructure across on-premise and cloud environments. You will be responsible for understanding requirements and designing, documenting, supporting and delivering secure, scalable and reliable solutions within a defined framework.&lt;br&gt;The successful candidate will collaborate with software development teams, project managers and infrastructure architects to design, build, deploy, operate and monitor enterprise applications and services. Responsibilities include implementing Infrastructure as Code (IaC), cloud automation, CI/CD pipelines, monitoring solutions and operational best practices.&lt;br&gt;This role requires hands-on experience with AWS services including ECS, EC2, RDS, S3, CloudFront, Lambda, Route 53, CloudWatch, IAM and networking services, as well as Windows and Linux administration. Experience with Azure DevOps, scripting, AI-assisted tools and automation is also desirable. Occasional work outside regular business hours is a requirement of the position. The role follows a hybrid work model, requiring employees to be onsite in the office 3 days per week and allowing remote work for the remaining days. Specific in-office days may be set by the team or department to support collaboration and business needs. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;padding:10.0px 0.0px;border:1.0px solid transparent&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:18.0px;word-wrap:break-word&quot;&gt;&lt;H2 style=&quot;font-size:1.0em;margin:0.0px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Duties and Responsibilities&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/H2&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, implement and support DevOps practices, cloud infrastructure, automation solutions and CI/CD pipelines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and maintain Infrastructure as Code and configuration management solutions using Terraform, AWS CloudFormation, Ansible or similar tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Configure, manage and troubleshoot AWS services including ECS, EC2, RDS, S3, CloudFront, Lambda, Route 53, CloudWatch, IAM, VPC and Elastic Load Balancing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and support containerized applications using Docker and Amazon ECS, and administer Windows and Linux environments across cloud and on-premise infrastructure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop automation and integrations using PowerShell, Python, YAML, REST APIs and related technologies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Implement monitoring, alerting, logging and performance optimization solutions for applications and infrastructure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Investigate and resolve application, infrastructure, networking, security and deployment issues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with development, infrastructure, security and business teams to deliver production-ready solutions that comply with City standards and industry best practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and maintain technical documentation, architecture diagrams, operational procedures and recovery plans.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evaluate emerging technologies, including AI-assisted DevOps tools and Microsoft Power Platform, to improve operational efficiency and service delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide technical guidance, training and knowledge transfer to staff and project teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in after-hours support, maintenance activities and emergency response as required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;padding:10.0px 0.0px;border:1.0px solid transparent&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:18.0px;word-wrap:break-word&quot;&gt;&lt;H2 style=&quot;font-size:1.0em;margin:0.0px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Skills and Qualifications&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/H2&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Post-secondary degree in Computer Science, Information Technology or a related discipline, or possess an equivalent combination of education, certifications and experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of experience as a DevOps Engineer, DevOps Specialist, Cloud Engineer or in a similar role.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of Agile methodologies, DevOps principles, source control and CI/CD practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing and implementing CI/CD pipelines using Azure DevOps, GitHub Actions, Jenkins or similar platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong experience configuring and supporting AWS environments, including ECS, EC2, RDS, S3, CloudFront, Lambda, Route 53, CloudWatch, IAM, VPC and load balancing services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Infrastructure as Code and configuration management tools such as Terraform, AWS CloudFormation, Ansible, Chef or Puppet.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Docker, Amazon ECS and containerized application delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong scripting and automation skills using PowerShell, Python and YAML.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Related IT certifications are an asset. AWS Certified DevOps Engineer, AWS Solutions Architect or equivalent is preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced hands-on experience with Windows and Linux administration, monitoring, logging and troubleshooting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent analytical, problem-solving, collaboration and documentation skills, with the ability to work independently or within cross-functional teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Microsoft Azure or other cloud platforms would be considered an asset.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience evaluating and implementing AI-assisted tools for software development, infrastructure operations and DevOps workflows would be considered an asset.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Microsoft Power Platform, including Power Apps and Power Automate, would be considered an asset.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;May require light lifting of supplies or materials and prolonged use of computer keyboards and screens in a primarily office-based environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0.0px;text-align:left&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt;Hourly Rate/Salary: $ 50.39 - $ 67.18 &lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt;Grade: TF &lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt;Hours of Work: 35 &lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt;Work Location: Civic Centre &lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;color:black&quot;&gt; Hybrid Workplace&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt;Organization Unit: CPS/Architecture, Projects &amp;amp; Cyb. Sec &lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt;Department/Division/Section: CPS/Corporate Services Dept , CPS/IT Division , Architecture, Projects &amp;amp; Cyb. Sec &lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt;Non-Union/Union: Non Union &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0.0px;text-align:left&quot;&gt; &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Applicants applying to this posting may be considered for the same position(s) should another vacancy occur within six months from the date of this posting, unless the requirement to repost is expressed differently in a Collective Agreement.&lt;br&gt;If you are selected for an interview and your proposed transfer or promotion results in a real or perceived conflict of interest in relation to the Employment of Relatives Corporate Policy and Procedure, you must notify the Human Resources Representative as soon as possible.&lt;br&gt;If you are selected for an interview you are expected to disclose all current positions held in the City, whether full time or part time.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI (Artificial Intelligence)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The City of Mississauga may use artificial intelligence (AI) technology in sourcing and/or screening candidates for some positions; however, it is not used in selecting final candidates&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Candidates are expected to complete interviews independently to ensure an equitable assessment. The use of AI-generated responses, AI assistants, transcription tools, or third-party coaching technologies during interviews is prohibited, unless supported by an approved accommodation and may result in disqualification from the recruitment process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Accommodations&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;The City of Mississauga is an Equal Opportunity Employer and is committed to removing barriers in our selection process for people with visible and invisible disabilities. In accordance with the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act, 2005 and the Ontario Human Rights Code, the City of Mississauga will provide accommodations throughout the recruitment, selection and/or assessment process to applicants with disabilities.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;If selected to participate in the recruitment, selection and/or assessment process, please complete the following &lt;a href=&quot;https://www7.mississauga.ca/documents/inside/talent/accommodation_request_form.pdf&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener&quot;&gt;Accommodation Request Form&lt;/a&gt; and have it emailed to &lt;a href=&quot;mailto:recruitment.accommodation@mississauga.ca&quot;&gt;recruitment.accommodation@mississauga.ca&lt;/a&gt; citing the Job ID and Job Title. This will inform Human Resources of the nature of any accommodation(s) that you may require in respect of any materials or processes used to ensure your equal participation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0.0px;text-align:left&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equity, Diversity and Inclusion&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;The City of Mississauga is committed to creating a respectful and supportive workplace that fosters a culture of equity, diversity and inclusion which broadly reflects the communities and residents we serve. Throughout the employee life cycle, the City is working to include an EDI lens to attract, retain and support the growth of diverse talent.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Learn more about the City’s commitment to &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.mississauga.ca/our-organization/equity-diversity-and-inclusion/&quot;&gt;Equity, Diversity and Inclusion&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:left&quot;&gt; &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:left&quot;&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://www7.mississauga.ca/documents/inside/talent/forbes_2026_footer_image.jpg&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; width=&quot;450&quot; height=&quot;101&quot;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:justify;margin:0.0&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt;Req ID: 27978&lt;br&gt;Vacancy Type: Temporary (2-yr contract with full benefits)&lt;br&gt;Number of Positions: 1  &lt;br&gt;Closing Date: 10/16/2026&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;padding:10.0px 0.0px;border:1.0px solid transparent&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:18.0px;word-wrap:break-word&quot;&gt;&lt;H2 style=&quot;font-size:1.0em;margin:0.0px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Job Summary&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/H2&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;The City of Mississauga is seeking an experienced Application Developer to support the modernization of the Property Tax Management system. The successful candidate will design, build, test, deploy, and support cloud-native web applications that replace legacy Oracle Forms and reports. We are looking for a pragmatic application developer who can translate complex taxation workflows, legacy PL/SQL logic, forms, and reports into maintainable digital products. The candidate should be comfortable working across frontends, backend, data, integration, security, and DevOps. You collaborate effectively with business analysts, architects, database specialists, security teams, infrastructure teams, vendors, and municipal partners, and you can balance modernization goals with business continuity and data integrity.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The role operates in a hybrid work environment, with office presence required at Mississauga City Hall, 300 City Centre Drive, Mississauga.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;padding:10.0px 0.0px;border:1.0px solid transparent&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:18.0px;word-wrap:break-word&quot;&gt;&lt;H2 style=&quot;font-size:1.0em;margin:0.0px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Duties and Responsibilities&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/H2&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Successful Candidate will: &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop accessible, responsive web interfaces using TypeScript and a modern frontend framework such as React or Angular. &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and maintain Java services, APIs, business rules, integrations, and batch-processing components supporting property-tax workflows. &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build reusable front-end components and RESTful APIs that follow API-first, modular and testable design principles. &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop containerized services on Amazon ECS and AWS Fargate, using Amazon S3 and DynamoDB for state management and asynchronous job processing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and implement RESTful APIs and reusable services that integrate frontend applications, workflow orchestration, databases, reporting components, and external systems. &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Implement asynchronous and scheduled processing for reports, calculations, file generation, data transformation, and other long-running jobs. &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build batch, scheduled-report and event-driven workflows using AWS Step Functions and container-based job processing. &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create and maintain automated unit, integration, API, end-to-end, regression, performance, and security tests. &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in the progressive migration of forms and reports while supporting coexistence between the modern AWS platform and the legacy environment. &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Apply role-based access control using Azure AD federation, AWS Cognito, JWT claims, and application-level authorization. &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to DevOps CI/CD pipelines, including static application security testing (SAST), code coverage, and pull-request review workflows. &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Protect data and secrets through TLS, encryption at rest, least-privilege IAM roles, AWS KMS, and AWS Secrets Manager. &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Investigate and resolve application defects, failed workflows, performance issues, integration errors, and production incidents. &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Produce technical designs, interface specifications, data mappings, runbooks, deployment instructions, test evidence, and support documentation. &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Estimate development effort, identify delivery risks, and contribute to sprint planning, backlog refinement, release planning, and technical governance. &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Follow the City’s SDLC and AI-SDLC standards: author specifications and steering files, review all AI-generated output, and stay accountable for submitted code. &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide operational support, knowledge transfer, and continuous enhancement for TXM applications and services. &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;padding:10.0px 0.0px;border:1.0px solid transparent&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:18.0px;word-wrap:break-word&quot;&gt;&lt;H2 style=&quot;font-size:1.0em;margin:0.0px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Skills and Qualifications&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/H2&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Post-secondary degree in Computer Science, Software Engineering, Information Technology, or a related discipline.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Minimum 3-5 years of experience developing enterprise applications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing applications using Java and object-oriented programming principles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with modern JavaScript/TypeScript development frameworks such as React, Angular, or Vue.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing and integrating RESTful APIs and web services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with AWS services like ECS Fargate, S3, Aurora DB, ALB, Cloudfront etc.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with relational databases and SQL preferably Postgre SQL.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with cloud-based application development (AWS preferred).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with source control, automated testing, and CI/CD practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of application security principles and secure coding practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical, problem-solving, and communication skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work independently and collaboratively within a team environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0.0px;text-align:left&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt;Hourly Rate/Salary: $ 49.16 - $ 65.54 &lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt;Grade: TF &lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt;Hours of Work:  &lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt;Work Location: Civic Centre &lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;color:black&quot;&gt; Hybrid Workplace &lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt;Organization Unit: CPS  &lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt;Department/Division/Section: CPS/Corporate Services Dept , CPS/IT Division , Enterprise Business Solutions &lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt;Non-Union/Union: Non Union &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0.0px;text-align:left&quot;&gt; &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0.0px;text-align:left&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt; The City of Mississauga may use artificial intelligence (AI) technology in sourcing candidates for some positions, however, it is not being used for screening, assessing, or selecting candidates. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:left&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt; Applicants applying to this posting may be considered for the same position(s) should another vacancy occur within six months from the date of this posting, unless the requirement to repost is expressed differently in a Collective Agreement. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt; If you are selected for an interview and your proposed transfer or promotion results in a real or perceived conflict of interest in relation to the Employment of Relatives Corporate Policy and Procedure, you must notify the Human Resources Representative as soon as possible. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt; If you are selected for an interview you are expected to disclose all current positions held in the City, whether full time or part time. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:left&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equity, Diversity and Inclusion&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt; The City of Mississauga is committed to creating a respectful and supportive workplace that fosters a culture of equity, diversity and inclusion which broadly reflects the communities and residents we serve. Throughout the employee life cycle, the City is working to include an EDI lens to attract, retain and support the growth of diverse talent. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt; Learn more about the City’s commitment to &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.mississauga.ca/our-organization/equity-diversity-and-inclusion/&quot;&gt;Equity, Diversity and Inclusion&lt;/a&gt;. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Accommodations&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt; The City of Mississauga is an Equal Opportunity Employer and is committed to removing barriers in our selection process for people with visible and invisible disabilities. In accordance with the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act, 2005 and the Ontario Human Rights Code, the City of Mississauga will provide accommodations throughout the recruitment, selection and/or assessment process to applicants with disabilities. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt; If selected to participate in the recruitment, selection and/or assessment process, please complete the following &lt;a title=&quot;&quot; href=&quot;https://www7.mississauga.ca/documents/inside/talent/accommodation_request_form.pdf&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener&quot;&gt;Accommodation Request Form&lt;/a&gt; and have it emailed to &lt;a href=&quot;mailto:recruitment.accommodation@mississauga.ca&quot;&gt;recruitment.accommodation@mississauga.ca&lt;/a&gt; citing the Job ID and Job Title. This will inform Human Resources of the nature of any accommodation(s) that you may require in respect of any materials or processes used to ensure your equal participation. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:left&quot;&gt; &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:left&quot;&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://www7.mississauga.ca/documents/inside/talent/forbes_2026_footer_image.jpg&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; width=&quot;450&quot; height=&quot;101&quot;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:justify&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt;Req ID: 28683 &lt;br&gt;Vacancy Type: Temporary &lt;br&gt;Contract Duration: January - April, 2027&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt;Number of Positions: 2  &lt;br&gt;Closing Date: 10/23/2026&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:justify&quot;&gt; &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:justify&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;To be considered for this competition, applicants must be enrolled in a recognized post‑secondary co-op program and be eligible to complete a Work Term during the specified period. Applicants must be legally eligible to work in Canada. Proof of enrolment in a related program must be uploaded when completing the application.&lt;/strong&gt;   &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;padding:10.0px 0.0px;border:1.0px solid transparent&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:18.0px;word-wrap:break-word&quot;&gt;&lt;H2 style=&quot;font-size:1.0em;margin:0.0px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Job Summary&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/H2&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Supports the Facilities Maintenance team by leading day-to-day improvements to its SharePoint environment. The role focuses on improving site navigation, content organization, document management, and access to information, including Power BI reports and dashboards. The position may also support other Facilities Maintenance activities, such as physical asset audits and inspections, CMMS database cleanup and validation, reporting, and standard operating procedures.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;padding:10.0px 0.0px;border:1.0px solid transparent&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:18.0px;word-wrap:break-word&quot;&gt;&lt;H2 style=&quot;font-size:1.0em;margin:0.0px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Duties and Responsibilities&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/H2&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Key duties and responsibilities include:&lt;br&gt;•    Improve and maintain the Facilities Maintenance SharePoint site, with emphasis on intuitive navigation, logical information architecture, usability, searchability, and consistent page design.&lt;br&gt;•    Create and update SharePoint pages, document libraries, lists, folders, metadata, views, links, permissions-related content requests, and other site content in accordance with established standards.&lt;br&gt;•    Review, reorganize, and maintain files and folders; identify outdated, duplicate, or misplaced content; and recommend practical improvements to document management.&lt;br&gt;•    Embed and organize Power BI reports and dashboards in SharePoint so operational and performance information is easy to find and use.&lt;br&gt;•    Gather user feedback, document business requirements, and implement practical improvements that increase SharePoint adoption and effectiveness.&lt;br&gt;•    May need to validate and update asset, equipment, location, and maintenance data in the CMMS, correcting incomplete, duplicate, outdated, or inconsistent records.&lt;br&gt;•    Support reports, dashboards, standard operating procedures, work instructions, templates, and other process documentation.&lt;br&gt;•    Conduct physical asset audits and cycle counts, compare findings with CMMS records, and reconcile identified discrepancies.&lt;br&gt;•    Perform other related duties in support of the Facilities Maintenance team as assigned.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;padding:10.0px 0.0px;border:1.0px solid transparent&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:18.0px;word-wrap:break-word&quot;&gt;&lt;H2 style=&quot;font-size:1.0em;margin:0.0px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Skills and Qualifications&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/H2&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;•    Currently enrolled in a university or college program related to information management, business technology, data analytics, asset management, engineering, facilities management, public administration, or a related field.&lt;br&gt;•    Good understanding of SharePoint, Power BI, database management. CMMS applications, maintenance planning, asset management, or data analysis is an asset.&lt;br&gt;•    Strong organizational skills, attention to detail, and commitment to data accuracy.&lt;br&gt;•    Ability to research, analyze, validate, and compile information into clear and usable formats.&lt;br&gt;•    Proficiency with Microsoft 365 applications; experience with SharePoint, Power BI, Excel, or similar reporting and collaboration tools is an asset.&lt;br&gt;•    Ability to organize digital information logically and consider the end-user experience when developing pages, libraries, folders, and navigation.&lt;br&gt;•    Strong written communication skills and the ability to assist in preparing reports, procedures, guides, and presentations.&lt;br&gt;•    Strong customer service, interpersonal, and verbal communication skills.&lt;br&gt;•    Ability to work independently, manage assigned tasks, exercise sound judgement, and collaborate effectively as part of a team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Working Conditions&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;•    Primarily office-based, with regular use of computers and Microsoft 365 applications.&lt;br&gt;•    Periodic field work at City facilities, including site inspections, physical asset verification, and cycle counts.&lt;br&gt;•    May require walking through mechanical, electrical, operational, storage, or other facility areas and light lifting of supplies or identification materials.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:left&quot;&gt;Hourly Rate/Salary: 20.64 - 24.53&lt;br&gt;Hours of Work: 35&lt;br&gt;Work Location: 950 Burnhamthorpe Rd W&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:red&quot;&gt; &lt;span style=&quot;color:black&quot;&gt;Hybrid Workplace &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;Organization Unit: CMS/Facilities Maintenance&lt;br&gt;Department/Division/Section: CMS/Community Services Dept , CMS/Facilities &amp;amp; Property Management , Facilities Maintenance&lt;br&gt;Non-Union/Union: Non Union&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Applicants applying to this posting may be considered for the same position(s) should another vacancy occur within six months from the date of this posting, unless the requirement to repost is expressed differently in a Collective Agreement.&lt;br&gt;If you are selected for an interview and your proposed transfer or promotion results in a real or perceived conflict of interest in relation to the Employment of Relatives Corporate Policy and Procedure, you must notify the Human Resources Representative as soon as possible.&lt;br&gt;If you are selected for an interview you are expected to disclose all current positions held in the City, whether full time or part time.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI (Artificial Intelligence)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The City of Mississauga may use artificial intelligence (AI) technology in sourcing and/or screening candidates for some positions; however, it is not used in selecting final candidates&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Candidates are expected to complete interviews independently to ensure an equitable assessment. The use of AI-generated responses, AI assistants, transcription tools, or third-party coaching technologies during interviews is prohibited, unless supported by an approved accommodation and may result in disqualification from the recruitment process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Accommodations&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;The City of Mississauga is an Equal Opportunity Employer and is committed to removing barriers in our selection process for people with visible and invisible disabilities. In accordance with the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act, 2005 and the Ontario Human Rights Code, the City of Mississauga will provide accommodations throughout the recruitment, selection and/or assessment process to applicants with disabilities.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;If selected to participate in the recruitment, selection and/or assessment process, please complete the following &lt;a href=&quot;https://www7.mississauga.ca/documents/inside/talent/accommodation_request_form.pdf&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener&quot;&gt;Accommodation Request Form&lt;/a&gt; and have it emailed to &lt;a href=&quot;mailto:recruitment.accommodation@mississauga.ca&quot;&gt;recruitment.accommodation@mississauga.ca&lt;/a&gt; citing the Job ID and Job Title. This will inform Human Resources of the nature of any accommodation(s) that you may require in respect of any materials or processes used to ensure your equal participation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0.0px;text-align:left&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equity, Diversity and Inclusion&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;The City of Mississauga is committed to creating a respectful and supportive workplace that fosters a culture of equity, diversity and inclusion which broadly reflects the communities and residents we serve. Throughout the employee life cycle, the City is working to include an EDI lens to attract, retain and support the growth of diverse talent.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Learn more about the City’s commitment to &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.mississauga.ca/our-organization/equity-diversity-and-inclusion/&quot;&gt;Equity, Diversity and Inclusion&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:left&quot;&gt; &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:left&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt; &lt;img src=&quot;https://www7.mississauga.ca/documents/inside/talent/forbes_2026_footer_image.jpg&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; width=&quot;450&quot; height=&quot;101&quot;&gt; &lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:justify;margin:0.0&quot;&gt;Req ID: 28656&lt;br&gt;Vacancy Type: Permanent &lt;br&gt;Number of Positions: 1  &lt;br&gt;Closing Date: 10/22/2026&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;padding:10.0px 0.0px;border:1.0px solid transparent&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:18.0px;word-wrap:break-word&quot;&gt;&lt;H2 style=&quot;font-size:1.0em;margin:0.0px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Job Summary&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/H2&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;This role reviews applications for building permits to confirm all building applications accepted and issued comply with the Ontario Building Code Act, Ontario Building Code, “applicable law” and are processed in accordance with the standards and requirements established in the Building By-law.  Accurately assess each proposal to determine applicable fees and charges and determine appropriate construction values.   &lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;padding:10.0px 0.0px;border:1.0px solid transparent&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:18.0px;word-wrap:break-word&quot;&gt;&lt;H2 style=&quot;font-size:1.0em;margin:0.0px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Duties and Responsibilities&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/H2&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Review &amp;amp; Assessment&lt;br&gt;•    Review and assess building permit application submissions in accordance with the Ontario Building Code Act, Building By-law , as well as other applicable law, department policies and procedures. &lt;br&gt;•    Review building permit applications to determine necessary approvals in accordance with applicable legislation and ensure compliance has been achieved prior to permit issuance.&lt;br&gt;•    Review and assess requests for conditional permits to determine eligibility and provide recommendations for management approval&lt;br&gt;•    Process building permit applications, including the review of documents, drawings and specifications for limited scope building permit applications to ensure compliance with the Building Code Act, Ontario Building Code, Building By-law, municipal by-laws and other applicable legislation as part of our express review services. Liaise with inspections staff to resolve design and construction issues and provide permit status&lt;br&gt;•    Coordinates and monitors approval process for projects subject to site plan approval and other applicable planning approvals.&lt;br&gt;•    Monitor application timelines to ensure compliance with prescribed timelines in the Ontario Building Code Act and take corrective action as necessary&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Interpretation&lt;br&gt;•    Accurately interpret and apply the Ontario Building Code Act, Ontario Building Code, Building by-law and other applicable legislation.&lt;br&gt;•    Interpret the Building Code Act, Building By-law and other applicable legislation as defined, to determine applicable fees and charges  &lt;br&gt;•    Performs research for and prepares technical reports as required or requested&lt;br&gt;•    Accurately provide professional advice on building permit applications and associated processes&lt;br&gt; &lt;br&gt;Data Entry &amp;amp; Record Keeping&lt;br&gt;•    Compile and maintain accurate records and associated documentation in accordance with established internal controls, protocols and legislation. &lt;br&gt;•    The accurate documentation is required in order to mitigate financial, reputation risks, and legal challenges. &lt;br&gt;•    Daily use of MAX, SharePoint, SAP and ePlans.&lt;br&gt; &lt;br&gt;Customer Service&lt;br&gt;•    Act as the principal point of contact throughout the building permit approval process for the public, applicants, City staff and external agencies.&lt;br&gt;•    Provide guidance and direction to applicants and internal stakeholders regarding building permit applications and associated approvals. Assists applicants in the coordination and expedition of building permit applications to ensure overall customer satisfaction.&lt;br&gt;•    Assists applicants in the facilitation of building permit issuance in compliance with prescribed timelines&lt;br&gt;•    Proactively build and maintain relationships with clients, able to provide clear, timely and transparent communication of information to facilitate timely building application approvals.&lt;br&gt; &lt;br&gt;Meetings&lt;br&gt;•    Attend meetings to discuss and provide advice regarding building permissions, approvals applicable legislation and associated processes. Conduct preliminary meetings and consultations advising applicants of the required approvals, documents, specifications and drawings required to facilitate building permit issuance and provide direction as to the necessary procedures and protocols. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;padding:10.0px 0.0px;border:1.0px solid transparent&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:18.0px;word-wrap:break-word&quot;&gt;&lt;H2 style=&quot;font-size:1.0em;margin:0.0px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Skills and Qualifications&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/H2&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;•    Undergraduate Degree or Community College Diploma in one or more of the following areas: Architecture, Engineering or related discipline &lt;br&gt;•    Registered Building Official with the Ministry of Municipal Affairs and Housing (MMAH)&lt;br&gt;•    Qualification in the following categories as defined under  Part 3, Division C of the Ontario Building Code from the Ministry of Municipal Affairs and Housing (MMAH) in the following categories: House, Small Buildings, General Legal Process, HVAC-House, Plumbing-House.  Qualification in additional categories would be considered an asset.&lt;br&gt;•    Eligibility for and willingness to obtain and maintain the Certified Building Code Official (CBCO) designation from the Ontario Building Officials Association (OBOA)&lt;br&gt;•    Thorough knowledge of the Building Code Act and Ontario Building Code&lt;br&gt;•    Working knowledge of Construction Regulations and Occupational Health and Safety Act&lt;br&gt;•    Working knowledge of the following principles and standards: building design and construction principles; building construction methods, building industry issues, trends and best practices.&lt;br&gt;•    Minimum of five years of related work experience reviewing and interpreting architectural drawings and policy documents or equivalent combination of education and experience &lt;br&gt;•    Knowledge of building and development application processes and associated legislation is highly preferred &lt;br&gt;•    Proficient in reading and interpreting drawings, specifications and other technical documents&lt;br&gt;•    Excellent verbal and written communication skills and interpersonal skills to effectively deal with the general public, consultants, developers, staff and others stakeholders within the building approvals process.&lt;br&gt;•    The ability to effectively communicate technical information to a non-technical audience is required&lt;br&gt;•    Well-developed analytical, research, organizational, negotiation and problem solving skills&lt;br&gt;•    Strong computer literacy is required with experience using MS Office and Adobe Acrobat; experience with Mississauga Approvals Express (MAX), EDMS, SharePoint, electronic plans submission (ePlans) or other permitting software is considered a strong asset&lt;br&gt;•    Must be flexible in adapting to rapidly changing workloads and work environments&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0.0px;text-align:left&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt;Hourly Rate/Salary: $ 80,567.00 - $ 107,426.00&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt;Hours of Work: 35&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt;Work Location: Civic Centre&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;color:black&quot;&gt;Hybrid Workplace&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt;Department/Division/Section: P&amp;amp;B/Planning &amp;amp; Building Dept , P&amp;amp;B/Building Division , Plan Examination Services&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt;Non-Union/Union: Non Union&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0.0px;text-align:left&quot;&gt; &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Applicants applying to this posting may be considered for the same position(s) should another vacancy occur within six months from the date of this posting, unless the requirement to repost is expressed differently in a Collective Agreement.&lt;br&gt;If you are selected for an interview and your proposed transfer or promotion results in a real or perceived conflict of interest in relation to the Employment of Relatives Corporate Policy and Procedure, you must notify the Human Resources Representative as soon as possible.&lt;br&gt;If you are selected for an interview you are expected to disclose all current positions held in the City, whether full time or part time.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI (Artificial Intelligence)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The City of Mississauga may use artificial intelligence (AI) technology in sourcing and/or screening candidates for some positions; however, it is not used in selecting final candidates&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Candidates are expected to complete interviews independently to ensure an equitable assessment. The use of AI-generated responses, AI assistants, transcription tools, or third-party coaching technologies during interviews is prohibited, unless supported by an approved accommodation and may result in disqualification from the recruitment process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Accommodations&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;The City of Mississauga is an Equal Opportunity Employer and is committed to removing barriers in our selection process for people with visible and invisible disabilities. In accordance with the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act, 2005 and the Ontario Human Rights Code, the City of Mississauga will provide accommodations throughout the recruitment, selection and/or assessment process to applicants with disabilities.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;If selected to participate in the recruitment, selection and/or assessment process, please complete the following &lt;a href=&quot;https://www7.mississauga.ca/documents/inside/talent/accommodation_request_form.pdf&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener&quot;&gt;Accommodation Request Form&lt;/a&gt; and have it emailed to &lt;a href=&quot;mailto:recruitment.accommodation@mississauga.ca&quot;&gt;recruitment.accommodation@mississauga.ca&lt;/a&gt; citing the Job ID and Job Title. This will inform Human Resources of the nature of any accommodation(s) that you may require in respect of any materials or processes used to ensure your equal participation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0.0px;text-align:left&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equity, Diversity and Inclusion&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;The City of Mississauga is committed to creating a respectful and supportive workplace that fosters a culture of equity, diversity and inclusion which broadly reflects the communities and residents we serve. Throughout the employee life cycle, the City is working to include an EDI lens to attract, retain and support the growth of diverse talent.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Learn more about the City’s commitment to &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.mississauga.ca/our-organization/equity-diversity-and-inclusion/&quot;&gt;Equity, Diversity and Inclusion&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
