&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://www7.mississauga.ca/documents/inside/talent/forbes_2026_footer_image.jpg&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; width=&quot;450&quot; height=&quot;101&quot;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:justify;margin:0.0&quot;&gt;Req ID: 28597&lt;br&gt;Vacancy Type: Permanent &lt;br&gt;Number of Positions: 1  &lt;br&gt;Closing Date: 10/16/2026&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;padding:10.0px 0.0px;border:1.0px solid transparent&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:18.0px;word-wrap:break-word&quot;&gt;&lt;H2 style=&quot;font-size:1.0em;margin:0.0px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Job Summary&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/H2&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Reporting to the Executive Manager of Development Engineering &amp;amp; Construction, the Supervisor of Traffic Planning leads a team of technical and professional staff in the review of development and permit applications, realty related requests and other roadway planning matters from a traffic planning perspective, including traffic impact studies, access modification permits, site plans, and pedestrian and vehicular circulation plans, while ensuring that best practices are followed and the City’s interests and objectives are maintained.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;padding:10.0px 0.0px;border:1.0px solid transparent&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:18.0px;word-wrap:break-word&quot;&gt;&lt;H2 style=&quot;font-size:1.0em;margin:0.0px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Duties and Responsibilities&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/H2&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration:underline&quot;&gt;Talent Management:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provides strategic vision, leadership, direction, professional/technical guidance, coaching and mentorship to the Traffic Planning team members;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manages and develops the performance of direct reports including recruitment, development of annual work plans, goals and objectives for each team member, and ensuring quality and production of each individual&apos;s work;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;On-boards and trains new staff;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Follows/tracks trends/changes regarding industry best practices and applicable regulatory regimes, forecasts pressures, and prepares business cases for resources as required; and,&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversees, directs and ensures the successful delivery of the Traffic Planning team&apos;s duties, responsibilities and workplan deliverables.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration:underline&quot;&gt;Ensuring Compliance:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversees and provides technical leadership to ensure the team’s review of the development applications, permits and realty request comply with guidelines, industry best practices, engineering standards, the City&apos;s Official Plan, the Planning Act and its regulations;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leads studies to update City guidelines, Zoning regulations, and other matters; and,&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensures the traffic planning process remains up to date by developing, implementing and continuously improving the team’s programs, processes, guidelines and standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration:underline&quot;&gt;Providing Expertise:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Regularly attends Planning and Development Committee meetings as a panelist to represent the Planning &amp;amp; Building Department and to provide expertise to the Committee on traffic planning matters;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Attends meetings with local Councillors, community members, the general public, outside agencies and other external and internal stakeholders as required to represent the City’s traffic planning interests, respond to questions and provide expertise;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leads workshops with inter/intra-departmental colleagues to develop solutions to new problems or conflicts related to the creation of new municipal roadways through the land development process; and,&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manages the review of very large and/or complex development applications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration:underline&quot;&gt;Monitoring and Reporting:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provides expertise and support related to road corridor and access management that include the authoring of corporate reports to the Leadership Team and Committees of Council;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensures coordinated and consistent reporting of issues and communications at all levels; and,&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversees the procurement and management of professional consulting services led by the team for the completion of traffic/transportation related studies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;padding:10.0px 0.0px;border:1.0px solid transparent&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:18.0px;word-wrap:break-word&quot;&gt;&lt;H2 style=&quot;font-size:1.0em;margin:0.0px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Skills and Qualifications&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/H2&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration:underline&quot;&gt;Education and Experience:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Post-secondary graduate from a recognized institution with a degree in Civil Engineering, Transportation Engineering or a related engineering or applied science program, or an equivalent combination of post-secondary education, qualifications and experience relevant to the role;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Professional engineering certification (P.Eng. or applicable Limited Engineering Licence) in good standing with Professional Engineers Ontario is preferred;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Minimum 8 years related experience with at least 3 years in a leadership role;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated project management experience; and,&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Municipal experience is considered to be an asset.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration:underline&quot;&gt;Knowledge and Expertise:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In-depth knowledge of traffic planning and traffic engineering principles, practices, guidelines and regulations;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Broad knowledge of the municipal land development process, including the Planning Act, the City&apos;s Official Plan, and the nuances of the various types of development applications; and&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of key principles traffic modelling, traffic safety, traffic control, roadway corridor management, active transportation, transportation demand management, roadway geometric design, capital planning, and other related disciplines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration:underline&quot;&gt;Competencies and Skills:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated leadership skills and ability to provide guidance and direction to staff while motivating and fostering a strong team;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent verbal and written communication skills, including the demonstrated ability to deliver presentations to technical and non-technical audiences;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong interpersonal, negotiation and collaboration skills, with a demonstrated ability to develop and foster effective working relationships;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated tact and diplomacy when dealing with the public and elected officials;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Effective decision making and problem solving skills with the ability to determine an effective course of action that drives progression;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong organizational skills with the ability to manage multiple competing tasks;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated competency in leadership, accountability, customer service, continuous improvement and City&apos;s core values - trust, quality and excellence; and,&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to provide self-transportation options to meetings and project sites within Mississauga and Peel.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0.0px;text-align:left&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt;Hourly Rate/Salary: $ 101,242.00 - $ 134,990.00&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt;Hours of Work: 35&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;color:black&quot;&gt;Work Location: Civic Centre&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;color:black&quot;&gt;Hybrid Workplace &lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt;Department/Division/Section: P&amp;amp;B/Planning &amp;amp; Building Dept , P&amp;amp;B/Building Division , Development Engineering &amp;amp; Constr&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt;Non-Union/Union: Non Union&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0.0px;text-align:left&quot;&gt; &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0.0px;text-align:left&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt;The City of Mississauga may use artificial intelligence (AI) technology in sourcing and/or screening candidates for some positions; however, it is not used in selecting final candidates. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt; We thank all who apply, however, only those candidates selected for an interview will be contacted. You can also check your application status in your candidate profile online. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt; All personal information is collected under the authority of the Municipal Act. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equity, Diversity and Inclusion&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt; The City of Mississauga is committed to creating a respectful and supportive workplace that fosters a culture of equity, diversity and inclusion which broadly reflects the communities and residents we serve. Throughout the employee life cycle, the City is working to include an EDI lens to attract, retain and support the growth of diverse talent. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt; Learn more about the City’s commitment to &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.mississauga.ca/our-organization/equity-diversity-and-inclusion/&quot;&gt;Equity, Diversity and Inclusion&lt;/a&gt;. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Accommodations&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt; The City of Mississauga is an Equal Opportunity Employer and is committed to removing barriers in our selection process for people with visible and invisible disabilities. In accordance with the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act, 2005 and the Ontario Human Rights Code, the City of Mississauga will provide accommodations throughout the recruitment, selection and/or assessment process to applicants with disabilities. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt; If selected to participate in the recruitment, selection and/or assessment process, please complete the following &lt;a title=&quot;&quot; href=&quot;https://www7.mississauga.ca/documents/inside/talent/accommodation_request_form.pdf&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener&quot;&gt;Accommodation Request Form&lt;/a&gt; and have it emailed to &lt;a href=&quot;mailto:recruitment.accommodation@mississauga.ca&quot;&gt;recruitment.accommodation@mississauga.ca&lt;/a&gt; citing the Job ID and Job Title. This will inform Human Resources of the nature of any accommodation(s) that you may require in respect of any materials or processes used to ensure your equal participation. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0.0px;text-align:left&quot;&gt; &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0.0px;text-align:left&quot;&gt; &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://www7.mississauga.ca/documents/inside/talent/forbes_2026_footer_image.jpg&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; width=&quot;450&quot; height=&quot;101&quot;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:justify;margin:0.0&quot;&gt;Req ID: 28666&lt;br&gt;Vacancy Type: Part-Time &lt;br&gt;Number of Positions: 5  &lt;br&gt;Closing Date: 12/18/2026&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;padding:10.0px 0.0px;border:1.0px solid transparent&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:18.0px;word-wrap:break-word&quot;&gt;&lt;H2 style=&quot;font-size:1.0em;margin:0.0px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Job Summary&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/H2&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Effectively plan and lead a group exercise format, specific to the outline provided.  The key result is for all participants to feel successful and positive, realizing value for time and quality in the product and experience. Lead, coach, provide guidance and motivation with the goal of the program to be safe, fun and effective.   &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;padding:10.0px 0.0px;border:1.0px solid transparent&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:18.0px;word-wrap:break-word&quot;&gt;&lt;H2 style=&quot;font-size:1.0em;margin:0.0px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Duties and Responsibilities&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/H2&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Creates a safe and effective class plan specific to the format outlined using sound training principles. &lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Include exercises and modifications that provide a variety of options for comfort and intensity to ensure that all participants feel safe and successful.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Plans and prepares music appropriate for the class format and the participants’ needs and preferences. &lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Present and instruct the group exercise format specific to the outline provided. &lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Provide verbal, visual and kinesthetic cueing for exercises and technique to appeal to a variety of learning styles. &lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Provide permission and options with verbal and/or visual demonstrations of options and modifications for exercises for comfort and to vary intensity.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Provide a combination of education and motivation appropriate to the format and participant group.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Engages with other staff with a positive and cooperative approach to best utilize facilities, space and serve participants. &lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Supports objectives and goals of all fitness programs through quality instruction, supervision and excellent customer and staff relations.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Conducts themselves inside and outside of the class in a positive and professional manner that is consistent with the City of Mississauga.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Promotes other classes and programs to encourage and inform participants. &lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Effectively provide quality customer service and act as a knowledgeable resource to participants&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Responds to customer needs and questions with accurate information and/or guidance to resources being responsible and acting within scope of knowledge and service.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Reaches out to the Supervisor or MOD when questions are beyond scope of service and specific to the facility and/or City of Mississauga programs and services. &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;padding:10.0px 0.0px;border:1.0px solid transparent&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:18.0px;word-wrap:break-word&quot;&gt;&lt;H2 style=&quot;font-size:1.0em;margin:0.0px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Skills and Qualifications&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/H2&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience teaching multi-level group exercise classes with a variety of formats&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Ability to demonstrate and perform physical exercises while instructing&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Work is performed primarily in a community centre environment&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Group Exercise Certification by a recognized association including Can Fit Pro, ACE, OFC or equivalent with annual renewals provided for validation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;A valid Basic First Aid (previously Emergency First Aid) and CPR B certification will be required of the successful candidate, as a condition of employment, at their own expense, prior to their start date&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A Level 3 – Vulnerable Check will be required of the successful candidate, as a condition of employment, at their own expense, to verify the absence of a criminal record for which a pardon has not been granted.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0.0px;text-align:left&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt;Hourly Rate/Salary: 34.90 - 39.89 &lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt;Grade: PH &lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt;Hours of Work: up to 24 &lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt;Work Location: Meadowvale CC &lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt;Organization Unit: CMS/Meadowvale Fitness &lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt;Department/Division/Section: CMS/Community Services Dept , CMS/Recreation &amp;amp; Culture Division , Program Delivery &lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt;Non-Union/Union: Non Union &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0.0px;text-align:left&quot;&gt; &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0.0px;text-align:left&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt;The City of Mississauga may use artificial intelligence (AI) technology in sourcing and/or screening candidates for some positions; however, it is not used in selecting final candidates. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:left&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt; Applicants applying to this posting may be considered for the same position(s) should another vacancy occur within six months from the date of this posting, unless the requirement to repost is expressed differently in a Collective Agreement. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt; If you are selected for an interview and your proposed transfer or promotion results in a real or perceived conflict of interest in relation to the Employment of Relatives Corporate Policy and Procedure, you must notify the Human Resources Representative as soon as possible. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt; If you are selected for an interview you are expected to disclose all current positions held in the City, whether full time or part time. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:left&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equity, Diversity and Inclusion&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt; The City of Mississauga is committed to creating a respectful and supportive workplace that fosters a culture of equity, diversity and inclusion which broadly reflects the communities and residents we serve. Throughout the employee life cycle, the City is working to include an EDI lens to attract, retain and support the growth of diverse talent. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt; Learn more about the City’s commitment to &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.mississauga.ca/our-organization/equity-diversity-and-inclusion/&quot;&gt;Equity, Diversity and Inclusion&lt;/a&gt;. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Accommodations&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt; The City of Mississauga is an Equal Opportunity Employer and is committed to removing barriers in our selection process for people with visible and invisible disabilities. In accordance with the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act, 2005 and the Ontario Human Rights Code, the City of Mississauga will provide accommodations throughout the recruitment, selection and/or assessment process to applicants with disabilities. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt; If selected to participate in the recruitment, selection and/or assessment process, please complete the following &lt;a title=&quot;&quot; href=&quot;https://www7.mississauga.ca/documents/inside/talent/accommodation_request_form.pdf&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener&quot;&gt;Accommodation Request Form&lt;/a&gt; and have it emailed to &lt;a href=&quot;mailto:recruitment.accommodation@mississauga.ca&quot;&gt;recruitment.accommodation@mississauga.ca&lt;/a&gt; citing the Job ID and Job Title. This will inform Human Resources of the nature of any accommodation(s) that you may require in respect of any materials or processes used to ensure your equal participation. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:left&quot;&gt; &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:left&quot;&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://www7.mississauga.ca/documents/inside/talent/forbes_2026_footer_image.jpg&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; width=&quot;450&quot; height=&quot;101&quot;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:justify;margin:0.0&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt;Req ID: 28636&lt;br&gt;Vacancy Type: Permanent &lt;br&gt;Number of Positions: 2  &lt;br&gt;Closing Date: 10/28/2026&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;padding:10.0px 0.0px;border:1.0px solid transparent&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:18.0px;word-wrap:break-word&quot;&gt;&lt;H2 style=&quot;font-size:1.0em;margin:0.0px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Job Summary&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/H2&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Asset Management Specialist leads the development, implementation and continuous improvement of the Enforcement Division’s asset management program, supporting a diverse portfolio of vehicles, technology, communications equipment, uniforms and specialized operational assets across eight regulatory and enforcement service areas.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The role provides strategic and operational leadership through the development of asset strategies, lifecycle and investment plans, governance frameworks, performance measures and business processes that support operational readiness, sustainability, accountability and effective resource allocation. Working collaboratively across corporate and operational teams, the Specialist provides subject matter expertise, oversees asset management systems and data, and leads initiatives that optimize asset performance and support front-line service delivery.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;padding:10.0px 0.0px;border:1.0px solid transparent&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:18.0px;word-wrap:break-word&quot;&gt;&lt;H2 style=&quot;font-size:1.0em;margin:0.0px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Duties and Responsibilities&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/H2&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the Division’s asset management program, including the development and implementation of strategies, policies, governance frameworks, standards, controls and performance measures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish and maintain consistent processes governing asset planning, acquisition, deployment, utilization, maintenance, replacement, transfer and disposal to support effective life cycle management and accountability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop lifecycle plans, replacement forecasts, multi-year asset plans, budget forecasts, business cases and funding recommendations to support long-term investment and resource allocation decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assess asset condition, utilization, criticality, risk, and lifecycle requirements to identify investment priorities, optimization opportunities, funding gaps and future asset needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead procurement planning and acquisition strategies, including requirements development, specification preparation, evaluations, contract administration, vendor management and warranty oversight.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Implement and oversee asset management systems, inventories and registries to ensure accurate asset data, effective tracking, lifecycle accountability and audit readiness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evaluate and optimize asset management technologies and related business processes to enhance asset visibility, system effectiveness and operational efficiency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop dashboards, performance measures and management reports and analyze financial, utilization, inventory and lifecycle data to identify trends, risks and opportunities for optimization and continuous improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct audits, reconciliations, risk assessments and benchmarking activities to strengthen governance, optimize asset performance and support informed decision-making.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide strategic advice and recommendations regarding asset investment, governance, procurement, lifecycle planning, operational risk and resource allocation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead stakeholder engagement, consultation and requirements gathering with Fleet Services, Finance, Procurement, IT, Materiel Management and operational partners to support coordinated asset planning and stewardship.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead cross-functional initiatives and represent the Division on corporate committees, working groups and enterprise projects to advance asset management objectives and operational effectiveness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate operational asset stewardship activities, including vehicles, inventories, assignments, transfers, recoveries, replenishment and compliance monitoring.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure governance, funding, procurement, training, tracking and life cycle controls are established to support the successful introduction of new programs, services, technologies and operational assets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Performing other duties, responsibilities and special projects as assigned.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;padding:10.0px 0.0px;border:1.0px solid transparent&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:18.0px;word-wrap:break-word&quot;&gt;&lt;H2 style=&quot;font-size:1.0em;margin:0.0px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Skills and Qualifications&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/H2&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Post-secondary degree or diploma in Business Administration, Public Administration, Asset Management, Supply Chain Management, Logistics, Operations Management, Information Technology, or related discipline.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Minimum of five (5) years of progressively responsible experience in asset management, program development, inventory management governance, fleet coordination, logistics, operational resource management or a related field, or an equivalent combination of education and relevant experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience developing and implementing asset management policies, governance frameworks, lifecycle strategies, internal controls, performance measures and continuous improvement initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience providing governance, planning or analytical support for a large, high-value and operationally diverse asset portfolio.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience conducting strategic planning, risk analysis, lifecycle forecasting, state-of-good repair reviews, inventory management, asset optimization, budget development and business case preparation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to assess financial exposure, operational consequences and organizational risk and translate complex findings into practical strategies, controls and recommendations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience administering or providing functional oversight of corporate or enterprise assets, inventory, fleet or technology-management systems, such as SAP, fleet management information systems, IT asset-tracking tools or equivalent platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated knowledge of data governance, asset registries, audit controls, performance measurement, management reporting and asset lifecycle data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong research, policy development, analytical, problem-solving and organizational skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to interpret corporate policies, operational requirements, technical information and industry best practices and develop appropriate divisional standards, procedures and processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced proficiency with Microsoft Office applications, particularly Excel, Word and PowerPoint, with the ability to analyze complex data, develop dashboards, prepare professional reports, presentations and business cases.  &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication skills, including the ability to explain complex information and present recommendations to management and stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong interpersonal, consultation and stakeholder management skills, with the ability to influence outcomes and establish effective working relationships across multiple business areas.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated project management and change management skills, with the ability to lead cross-functional initiatives involving competing priorities, multiple stakeholders and complex operational requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to exercise independent judgement, manage sensitive information and work with minimal supervision in a complex, high-accountability environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of municipal procurement, inventory management, fleet operations, and asset optimization and management best practices is considered an asset.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of LEAN principles and continuous improvement methodologies is considered an asset.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Certification in Asset Management, Supply Chain Management, Project Management or a related discipline is considered an asset.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Valid Ontario Class G Driver’s Licence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0.0px;text-align:left&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt;Hourly Rate/Salary: $ 80,567.00 - $ 107,426.00&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt;Hours of Work: 35&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt;Work Location: 950 Burnhamthorpe Rd W&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt;Department/Division/Section: CMS/Community Services Dept , CMS/Enforcement Division , Strategic Ops, Compliance &amp;amp; Enf&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt;Non-Union/Union: Non Union&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0.0px;text-align:left&quot;&gt; &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Applicants applying to this posting may be considered for the same position(s) should another vacancy occur within six months from the date of this posting, unless the requirement to repost is expressed differently in a Collective Agreement.&lt;br&gt;If you are selected for an interview and your proposed transfer or promotion results in a real or perceived conflict of interest in relation to the Employment of Relatives Corporate Policy and Procedure, you must notify the Human Resources Representative as soon as possible.&lt;br&gt;If you are selected for an interview you are expected to disclose all current positions held in the City, whether full time or part time.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI (Artificial Intelligence)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The City of Mississauga may use artificial intelligence (AI) technology in sourcing and/or screening candidates for some positions; however, it is not used in selecting final candidates&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Candidates are expected to complete interviews independently to ensure an equitable assessment. The use of AI-generated responses, AI assistants, transcription tools, or third-party coaching technologies during interviews is prohibited, unless supported by an approved accommodation and may result in disqualification from the recruitment process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Accommodations&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;The City of Mississauga is an Equal Opportunity Employer and is committed to removing barriers in our selection process for people with visible and invisible disabilities. In accordance with the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act, 2005 and the Ontario Human Rights Code, the City of Mississauga will provide accommodations throughout the recruitment, selection and/or assessment process to applicants with disabilities.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;If selected to participate in the recruitment, selection and/or assessment process, please complete the following &lt;a href=&quot;https://www7.mississauga.ca/documents/inside/talent/accommodation_request_form.pdf&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener&quot;&gt;Accommodation Request Form&lt;/a&gt; and have it emailed to &lt;a href=&quot;mailto:recruitment.accommodation@mississauga.ca&quot;&gt;recruitment.accommodation@mississauga.ca&lt;/a&gt; citing the Job ID and Job Title. This will inform Human Resources of the nature of any accommodation(s) that you may require in respect of any materials or processes used to ensure your equal participation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0.0px;text-align:left&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equity, Diversity and Inclusion&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;The City of Mississauga is committed to creating a respectful and supportive workplace that fosters a culture of equity, diversity and inclusion which broadly reflects the communities and residents we serve. Throughout the employee life cycle, the City is working to include an EDI lens to attract, retain and support the growth of diverse talent.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Learn more about the City’s commitment to &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.mississauga.ca/our-organization/equity-diversity-and-inclusion/&quot;&gt;Equity, Diversity and Inclusion&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0.0px;text-align:left&quot;&gt; &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0.0px;text-align:left&quot;&gt; &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://www7.mississauga.ca/documents/inside/talent/forbes_2026_footer_image.jpg&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; width=&quot;450&quot; height=&quot;101&quot;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:justify;margin:0.0&quot;&gt;Req ID: 28668&lt;br&gt;Vacancy Type: Permanent &lt;br&gt;Contract Duration: &lt;br&gt;Number of Positions: 5  &lt;br&gt;Closing Date: 10/30/2026&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;padding:10.0px 0.0px;border:1.0px solid transparent&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:18.0px;word-wrap:break-word&quot;&gt;&lt;H2 style=&quot;font-size:1.0em;margin:0.0px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Job Summary&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/H2&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Working for the City means you are part of something big, something special! You will be part or a team of engaging, enthusiastic and dedicated people that are committed to collaborating with one another to deliver on our commitment to the residents, visitors and businesses of Mississauga.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;padding:10.0px 0.0px;border:1.0px solid transparent&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:18.0px;word-wrap:break-word&quot;&gt;&lt;H2 style=&quot;font-size:1.0em;margin:0.0px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Duties and Responsibilities&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/H2&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration:underline&quot;&gt;Exercise Counsellor:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul style=&quot;list-style-type:disc&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Responsible for demonstrating proper instruction to customers with respect to correct technique and use of exercise equipment. &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Responsible for enforcing fitness etiquette rules and guidelines posted.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist customer service with facility tours, provide direction, and clear all applicable areas in emergency situations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform daily safety inspections, inventories and cleaning duties. &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Responsible for checking wristbands for select fitness classes as needed. &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide emergency first-aid when required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provides Fitness Starters (45 mins) to members who have signed up. &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Counsellor will show select cardio and strength exercises, takes blood pressure, heart rate and will provide quality customer service and act as a knowledgeable resource to participants.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration:underline&quot;&gt;Personal Trainer, Fitness:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul style=&quot;list-style-type:disc&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Responsible for contacting clients to arrange training/assessment times.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Responsible for reviewing Personal Training request sheet and Par Q health screening questionnaire.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide Fitness Assessments for effective customer screening and program design.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must have knowledge of PAR Q interpretation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide assessments (approx.1 hour in duration) and focus on body composition, customer goals, blood pressure/heart rate screening, strength, flexibility and cardiovascular health.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Responsible for program design/exercise prescription specific to client’s individual goals, needs, limitations and must stay within scope of practice for effective program design.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor and correct technique throughout exercise session and effectively adjust program based on needs and plateau peaks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Continually provide encouragement and support to clients and strive to provide a safe and effective environment for clients and surrounding members.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Modify exercises with respect to principles of training for effective program delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;padding:10.0px 0.0px;border:1.0px solid transparent&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:18.0px;word-wrap:break-word&quot;&gt;&lt;H2 style=&quot;font-size:1.0em;margin:0.0px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Skills and Qualifications&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/H2&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Personal Training Certificate by a recognized association including Can Fit Pro, ACE, ACSM, NSCA, CPTN or equivalent with annual renewals provided for validation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Completion of a minimum 2 years of a College Diploma/University Degree program in a fitness related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt; A valid Basic First Aid (previously Emergency First Aid) and CPR B certification or Immediate First Aid (previously Standard First Aid) and CPR C certification is required prior to your start date.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience and familiarity with common fitness training techniques.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong program leadership skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Level 3 – Vulnerable check will be required of the successful candidate, as a condition of employment, at their own expense, to verify the absence of a criminal record for which a pardon has not been granted.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:left&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt; Hourly Rate/Salary: 24.02- 26.41 &lt;br&gt;Grade: PD &lt;br&gt;Hours of Work: up to 24 &lt;br&gt;Work Location: Various &lt;br&gt;Organization Unit: CMS/Meadowvale Fitness &lt;br&gt;Department/Division/Section: CMS/Community Services Dept , CMS/Recreation &amp;amp; Culture Division , Program Delivery &lt;br&gt;Non-Union/Union: Non Union &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Applicants applying to this posting may be considered for the same position(s) should another vacancy occur within six months from the date of this posting, unless the requirement to repost is expressed differently in a Collective Agreement.&lt;br&gt;If you are selected for an interview and your proposed transfer or promotion results in a real or perceived conflict of interest in relation to the Employment of Relatives Corporate Policy and Procedure, you must notify the Human Resources Representative as soon as possible.&lt;br&gt;If you are selected for an interview you are expected to disclose all current positions held in the City, whether full time or part time.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI (Artificial Intelligence)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The City of Mississauga may use artificial intelligence (AI) technology in sourcing and/or screening candidates for some positions; however, it is not used in selecting final candidates&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Candidates are expected to complete interviews independently to ensure an equitable assessment. The use of AI-generated responses, AI assistants, transcription tools, or third-party coaching technologies during interviews is prohibited, unless supported by an approved accommodation and may result in disqualification from the recruitment process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Accommodations&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;The City of Mississauga is an Equal Opportunity Employer and is committed to removing barriers in our selection process for people with visible and invisible disabilities. In accordance with the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act, 2005 and the Ontario Human Rights Code, the City of Mississauga will provide accommodations throughout the recruitment, selection and/or assessment process to applicants with disabilities.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;If selected to participate in the recruitment, selection and/or assessment process, please complete the following &lt;a href=&quot;https://www7.mississauga.ca/documents/inside/talent/accommodation_request_form.pdf&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener&quot;&gt;Accommodation Request Form&lt;/a&gt; and have it emailed to &lt;a href=&quot;mailto:recruitment.accommodation@mississauga.ca&quot;&gt;recruitment.accommodation@mississauga.ca&lt;/a&gt; citing the Job ID and Job Title. This will inform Human Resources of the nature of any accommodation(s) that you may require in respect of any materials or processes used to ensure your equal participation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0.0px;text-align:left&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equity, Diversity and Inclusion&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;The City of Mississauga is committed to creating a respectful and supportive workplace that fosters a culture of equity, diversity and inclusion which broadly reflects the communities and residents we serve. Throughout the employee life cycle, the City is working to include an EDI lens to attract, retain and support the growth of diverse talent.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Learn more about the City’s commitment to &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.mississauga.ca/our-organization/equity-diversity-and-inclusion/&quot;&gt;Equity, Diversity and Inclusion&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:left&quot;&gt; &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://www7.mississauga.ca/documents/inside/talent/forbes_2026_footer_image.jpg&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; width=&quot;450&quot; height=&quot;101&quot;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:justify&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:10.0pt;color:black&quot;&gt;Req ID: 28671&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:10.0pt;color:black&quot;&gt;Vacancy Type: Part-Time &lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:10.0pt;color:black&quot;&gt;Number of Positions: 10  &lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:10.0pt;color:black&quot;&gt;Closing Date: 10/16/2026&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;padding:10.0px 0.0px;border:1.0px solid transparent&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:18.0px;word-wrap:break-word&quot;&gt;&lt;H2 style=&quot;font-size:1.0em;margin:0.0px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Job Summary&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/H2&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:10.0pt;color:black&quot;&gt;The City of Mississauga is a dynamic place to work; we have a culture that is engaging, vibrant, optimistic, collaborative, and effective. We live by our core values of trust, quality and excellence. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:10.0pt;color:black&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Please note:&lt;/strong&gt; This posting will be used to fill various vacancies over the coming months and therefore interviews will be offered when required. The recruitment of these positions is dependent on available vacancies and business needs. Scheduled hours are determined by facility and business needs and may vary from one facility to another.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;padding:10.0px 0.0px;border:1.0px solid transparent&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:18.0px;word-wrap:break-word&quot;&gt;&lt;H2 style=&quot;font-size:1.0em;margin:0.0px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Duties and Responsibilities&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/H2&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:10.0pt;color:black&quot;&gt;Under the direction of the Supervisor, Community Programs and with functional guidance from the Recreation Programmer, the successful candidate will develop various means of communication with youth to foster a youth-friendly centre that is responsive to the needs of youth in the community. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:10.0pt;color:black&quot;&gt;To support the vision and principles of the City of Mississauga&apos;s Youth Friendly Culture.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:10.0pt;color:black&quot;&gt;Raise awareness and involvement for youth within the community by supporting outreach and connecting with local schools as identified by the Supervisor of Community Porgrams, to provide information about youth-friendly activities and community resources.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:10.0pt;color:black&quot;&gt;To develop, maintain and mentor youth-led advisory group volunteers at the centre that will lead peer to peer activities and provide feedback on city services on a regular basis.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:10.0pt;color:black&quot;&gt;Provide mentorship and guidance for youth-driven and youth-led events and activities.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:10.0pt;color:black&quot;&gt;To maintain a youth friendly environment in the lobby and common areas of the community centre and develop a strong understanding of issues and barriers affecting youth participation.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:10.0pt;color:black&quot;&gt;Will act as a resource to the community centre in relation to positive youth engagement providing insight and guidance on youth related matters and ideas on how best to meet the needs of youth in the community.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:10.0pt;color:black&quot;&gt;Engage youth (ages 10-24) who access the community centre and within the community to assist them in engaging in recreation services, accessing community resources available to them.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:10.0pt;color:black&quot;&gt;Responsible for the accurate collection and reporting of youth program participant statistics.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:10.0pt;color:black&quot;&gt;Perform other related duties as assigned.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;padding:10.0px 0.0px;border:1.0px solid transparent&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:18.0px;word-wrap:break-word&quot;&gt;&lt;H2 style=&quot;font-size:1.0em;margin:0.0px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Skills and Qualifications&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/H2&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:10.0pt;color:black&quot;&gt;Must be at least 16 years of age or older&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:10.0pt;color:black&quot;&gt;Post-secondary degree or diploma in Social Sciences, Child &amp;amp; Youth Worker, Community Development or equivalent work experience in youth services field.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:10.0pt;color:black&quot;&gt;Demonstrated experience working with youth from diverse backgrounds with knowledge of social service, educational and youth services resources within Peel is an asset.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:10.0pt;color:black&quot;&gt;Demonstrated experience working with at-risk youth and/or street-involved people (primarily in a community centre environment) is considered an asset. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:10.0pt;color:black&quot;&gt;Must hold a valid and current Intermediate First Aid or Standard First Aid certification with CPR C &amp;amp; AED from a recognized WSIB-provider or must hold a valid and current Basic First Aid or Emergency First Aid with CPR C &amp;amp; AED from a recognized WSIB-provider, at the employee’s expense.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:10.0pt;color:black&quot;&gt;Must hold a valid HIGH FIVE ® Principles of Healthy Child Development certification and is at the employee’s expense. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:10.0pt;color:black&quot;&gt;Must be available to work a flexible schedule, including days, evenings, and weekends, based on program and operational requirements.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:10.0pt;color:black&quot;&gt;A Level 3 - Vulnerable Sector Check will be required of the successful candidate, as a condition of employment, at their own expense, to verify the absence of a criminal record for which a pardon has not been granted.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:left&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:10.0pt;color:black&quot;&gt;Hourly Rate/Salary: 21.64 - 26.41 &lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:10.0pt;color:black&quot;&gt;Grade: PD &lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:10.0pt;color:black&quot;&gt;Hours of Work: up to 24 hours per week. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:10.0pt;color:black&quot;&gt;Work Location: Various Locations &lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:10.0pt;color:black&quot;&gt;Department/Division/Section: CMS/Community Services Dept , CMS/Recreation &amp;amp; Culture Division  &lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:10.0pt;color:black&quot;&gt;Non-Union/Union: Non Union &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:left&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:10.0pt;color:black&quot;&gt;The City of Mississauga may use artificial intelligence (AI) technology in sourcing and/or screening candidates for some positions; however, it is not used in selecting final candidates. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:left&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:10.0pt;color:black&quot;&gt; Applicants applying to this posting may be considered for the same position(s) should another vacancy occur within six months from the date of this posting, unless the requirement to repost is expressed differently in a Collective Agreement. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:10.0pt;color:black&quot;&gt; If you are selected for an interview and your proposed transfer or promotion results in a real or perceived conflict of interest in relation to the Employment of Relatives Corporate Policy and Procedure, you must notify the Human Resources Representative as soon as possible. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:10.0pt;color:black&quot;&gt; If you are selected for an interview you are expected to disclose all current positions held in the City, whether full time or part time. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:10.0pt;color:black&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equity, Diversity and Inclusion&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:10.0pt;color:black&quot;&gt; The City of Mississauga is committed to creating a respectful and supportive workplace that fosters a culture of equity, diversity and inclusion which broadly reflects the communities and residents we serve. Throughout the employee life cycle, the City is working to include an EDI lens to attract, retain and support the growth of diverse talent. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:10.0pt;color:black&quot;&gt; Learn more about the City’s commitment to &lt;a style=&quot;color:black&quot; href=&quot;https://www.mississauga.ca/our-organization/equity-diversity-and-inclusion/&quot;&gt; Equity, Diversity and Inclusion &lt;/a&gt;. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:10.0pt;color:black&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Accommodations&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:left&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:10.0pt;color:black&quot;&gt; The City of Mississauga is an Equal Opportunity Employer and is committed to removing barriers in our selection process for people with visible and invisible disabilities. In accordance with the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act, 2005 and the Ontario Human Rights Code, the City of Mississauga will provide accommodations throughout the recruitment, selection and/or assessment process to applicants with disabilities. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:10.0pt;color:black&quot;&gt; If selected to participate in the recruitment, selection and/or assessment process, please complete the following &lt;a style=&quot;color:black&quot; title=&quot;&quot; href=&quot;https://www7.mississauga.ca/documents/inside/talent/accommodation_request_form.pdf&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener&quot;&gt; Accommodation Request Form &lt;/a&gt; and have it emailed to &lt;a style=&quot;color:black&quot; href=&quot;mailto:recruitment.accommodation@mississauga.ca&quot;&gt;recruitment.accommodation@mississauga.ca&lt;/a&gt; citing the Job ID and Job Title. This will inform Human Resources of the nature of any accommodation(s) that you may require in respect of any materials or processes used to ensure your equal participation. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:left&quot;&gt; &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:justify&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:10.0pt;color:black&quot;&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://www7.mississauga.ca/documents/inside/talent/forbes_2026_footer_image.jpg&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; width=&quot;450&quot; height=&quot;101&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:justify&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt;Req ID: 28676 &lt;br&gt;Vacancy Type: Temporary &lt;br&gt;Contract Duration: January - April, 2027&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt;Number of Positions: 1  &lt;br&gt;Closing Date: 10/21/2026&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:justify&quot;&gt; &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:justify&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;To be considered for this competition, applicants must be enrolled in a recognized post‑secondary co-op program and be eligible to complete a Work Term during the specified period. Applicants must be legally eligible to work in Canada. Proof of enrolment in a related program must be uploaded when completing the application.&lt;/strong&gt;    &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;padding:10.0px 0.0px;border:1.0px solid transparent&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:18.0px;word-wrap:break-word&quot;&gt;&lt;H2 style=&quot;font-size:1.0em;margin:0.0px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Job Summary&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/H2&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;The WordPress Developer Co-op Student will support the development, maintenance, testing, and continuous improvement of the organization’s WordPress websites and digital platforms. Working under the guidance of experienced team members, the student will assist with WordPress configuration, content management, troubleshooting, quality assurance, accessibility, and web development activities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The role provides hands-on experience working in a professional web development environment and exposure to WordPress, PHP, HTML, CSS, JavaScript, APIs, cloud technologies, accessibility standards, domain management, DNS configuration, SSL certificates, and development workflows. Exposure to Vue.js may also be provided depending on project needs.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;padding:10.0px 0.0px;border:1.0px solid transparent&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:18.0px;word-wrap:break-word&quot;&gt;&lt;H2 style=&quot;font-size:1.0em;margin:0.0px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Duties and Responsibilities&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/H2&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;• Assist with day-to-day WordPress website maintenance and support.&lt;br&gt;• Assist with creating and updating WordPress pages, templates, themes, and plugins.&lt;br&gt;• Support front-end development using HTML, CSS, and JavaScript.&lt;br&gt;• Assist with basic PHP and WordPress development tasks.&lt;br&gt;• Gain experience working with Advanced Custom Fields (ACF).&lt;br&gt;• Assist with website testing, troubleshooting, and bug identification.&lt;br&gt;• Assist with accessibility testing and remediation, including WCAG-related requirements.&lt;br&gt;• Support WordPress plugin and core update testing.&lt;br&gt;• Gain exposure to APIs, AWS/Azure, domains, DNS, HTTPS, and SSL certificates.&lt;br&gt;• May gain exposure to Vue.js depending on project requirements.&lt;br&gt;• Assist with technical documentation, task tracking, and research.&lt;br&gt;• Participate in team meetings and collaborate with development team members.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;padding:10.0px 0.0px;border:1.0px solid transparent&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:18.0px;word-wrap:break-word&quot;&gt;&lt;H2 style=&quot;font-size:1.0em;margin:0.0px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Skills and Qualifications&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/H2&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;• Currently enrolled in a University or College program related to Computer Science, Software Development, Web Development, Information Technology, or a related field.&lt;br&gt;• Basic knowledge of HTML, CSS, and web development concepts.&lt;br&gt;• Exposure to WordPress, JavaScript, or PHP is considered an asset.&lt;br&gt;• Exposure to Vue.js is considered an asset but is not required.&lt;br&gt;• Exposure to Git, AWS/Azure, APIs, DNS, or SSL is considered an asset.&lt;br&gt;• Basic awareness of web accessibility or WCAG standards is considered an asset.&lt;br&gt;• Strong willingness to learn and develop new technical skills.&lt;br&gt;• Good problem-solving, communication, and teamwork skills.&lt;br&gt;• Strong attention to detail.&lt;br&gt;• Primarily an office and computer-based environment.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:left&quot;&gt;Hourly Rate/Salary: 20.64 - 24.53&lt;br&gt;Hours of Work: 35&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:black&quot;&gt;Work Location: Civic Centre&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:black&quot;&gt;Hybrid Workplace&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;Organization Unit: CPS/Net &amp;amp; Custom Apps&lt;br&gt;Department/Division/Section: CPS/Corporate Services Dept , CPS/IT Division , Enterprise Business Solutions&lt;br&gt;Non-Union/Union: Non Union&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Applicants applying to this posting may be considered for the same position(s) should another vacancy occur within six months from the date of this posting, unless the requirement to repost is expressed differently in a Collective Agreement.&lt;br&gt;If you are selected for an interview and your proposed transfer or promotion results in a real or perceived conflict of interest in relation to the Employment of Relatives Corporate Policy and Procedure, you must notify the Human Resources Representative as soon as possible.&lt;br&gt;If you are selected for an interview you are expected to disclose all current positions held in the City, whether full time or part time.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI (Artificial Intelligence)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The City of Mississauga may use artificial intelligence (AI) technology in sourcing and/or screening candidates for some positions; however, it is not used in selecting final candidates&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Candidates are expected to complete interviews independently to ensure an equitable assessment. The use of AI-generated responses, AI assistants, transcription tools, or third-party coaching technologies during interviews is prohibited, unless supported by an approved accommodation and may result in disqualification from the recruitment process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Accommodations&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;The City of Mississauga is an Equal Opportunity Employer and is committed to removing barriers in our selection process for people with visible and invisible disabilities. In accordance with the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act, 2005 and the Ontario Human Rights Code, the City of Mississauga will provide accommodations throughout the recruitment, selection and/or assessment process to applicants with disabilities.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;If selected to participate in the recruitment, selection and/or assessment process, please complete the following &lt;a href=&quot;https://www7.mississauga.ca/documents/inside/talent/accommodation_request_form.pdf&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener&quot;&gt;Accommodation Request Form&lt;/a&gt; and have it emailed to &lt;a href=&quot;mailto:recruitment.accommodation@mississauga.ca&quot;&gt;recruitment.accommodation@mississauga.ca&lt;/a&gt; citing the Job ID and Job Title. This will inform Human Resources of the nature of any accommodation(s) that you may require in respect of any materials or processes used to ensure your equal participation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0.0px;text-align:left&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equity, Diversity and Inclusion&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;The City of Mississauga is committed to creating a respectful and supportive workplace that fosters a culture of equity, diversity and inclusion which broadly reflects the communities and residents we serve. Throughout the employee life cycle, the City is working to include an EDI lens to attract, retain and support the growth of diverse talent.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Learn more about the City’s commitment to &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.mississauga.ca/our-organization/equity-diversity-and-inclusion/&quot;&gt;Equity, Diversity and Inclusion&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:left&quot;&gt; &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:left&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt; &lt;img src=&quot;https://www7.mississauga.ca/documents/inside/talent/forbes_2026_footer_image.jpg&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; width=&quot;450&quot; height=&quot;101&quot;&gt; &lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:justify;margin:0.0&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt;Req ID: 28672&lt;br&gt;Vacancy Type: Permanent &lt;br&gt;Number of Positions: 1  &lt;br&gt;Closing Date: 11/05/2026&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;padding:10.0px 0.0px;border:1.0px solid transparent&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:18.0px;word-wrap:break-word&quot;&gt;&lt;H2 style=&quot;font-size:1.0em;margin:0.0px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Job Summary&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/H2&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Do you want to be part of the team that brings a cultural shift towards multi-modal transportation in Mississauga? If so, Transportation Planning is looking for a Project Leader that will create and implement long-range transportation plans and establish a city-wide framework for multi-modal transportation.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;padding:10.0px 0.0px;border:1.0px solid transparent&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:18.0px;word-wrap:break-word&quot;&gt;&lt;H2 style=&quot;font-size:1.0em;margin:0.0px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Duties and Responsibilities&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/H2&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Under the direction of the Manager, Transportation Planning, this position will:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Undertake multi-modal transportation projects to implement the City’s Transportation Master Plan (TMP) in partnership with the appropriate City staff, other transportation agencies, funding partners and/or stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Undertake Corridor Transportation Master Plans, City-wide transportation studies and area-specific transportation reviews&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Initiate the development and monitoring of City-wide transportation policies for the City’s Official Plan, ensuring the necessary supporting research and technical analysis is undertaken&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Undertake the Development Charges Transportation Background Study in consultation with other sections, divisions and departments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide support for the annual budgeting process as it relates to section, divisional and departmental projects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review local, national, and international best practices on transportation planning matters, with a view to guiding the development and advancement of the City’s transportation system&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent the section and/or department on inter-departmental and inter-agency projects, attending public meetings, giving presentations and answering questions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare presentations, briefing memos, corporate reports and other correspondence for senior city staff and members of City Council and Committees of Council on transportation planning matters&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform other related duties as assigned&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;padding:10.0px 0.0px;border:1.0px solid transparent&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:18.0px;word-wrap:break-word&quot;&gt;&lt;H2 style=&quot;font-size:1.0em;margin:0.0px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Skills and Qualifications&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/H2&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A graduate from a recognized university program in transportation planning, civil engineering or related program with a minimum of 5 years of experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Membership or eligibility for membership as a professional engineer or in the Ontario Professional Planners Institute&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated strong project management and ability to multi-task, prioritize and adapt quickly to change&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Key job competencies are acting with integrity, communicating effectively, driving continuous improvement, serving customers, resolving conflict, driving projects to completion and thinking broadly&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Good working knowledge of transportation planning theories, principles and analysis techniques&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong working knowledge of related disciplines such as the environmental assessment process, land use planning and traffic and transit operations is an asset&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of Provincial, Regional, GTA and City transportation policy context and key trends that influence and shape the city&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0.0px;text-align:left&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt;Hourly Rate/Salary: $ 101,242.00 - $ 134,990.00&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt;Hours of Work: 35&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt;Work Location: Civic Centre&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;Work Model: &lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;color:black&quot;&gt;This role follows a hybrid work model, requiring employees to be onsite in the office 3 days per week and allowing remote work for the remaining days. Specific in-office days may be set by the team or department to support collaboration and business needs. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;color:black&quot;&gt;Department/Division/Section: T&amp;amp;W/Transportation&amp;amp;Works Dept , T&amp;amp;W/Infrast Planning &amp;amp; Eng Serv Div , Transportation Planning&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt;Non-Union/Union: Non Union&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0.0px;text-align:left&quot;&gt; &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0.0px;text-align:left&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt;The City of Mississauga may use artificial intelligence (AI) technology in sourcing and/or screening candidates for some positions; however, it is not used in selecting final candidates. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt; We thank all who apply, however, only those candidates selected for an interview will be contacted. You can also check your application status in your candidate profile online. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt; All personal information is collected under the authority of the Municipal Act. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equity, Diversity and Inclusion&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt; The City of Mississauga is committed to creating a respectful and supportive workplace that fosters a culture of equity, diversity and inclusion which broadly reflects the communities and residents we serve. Throughout the employee life cycle, the City is working to include an EDI lens to attract, retain and support the growth of diverse talent. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt; Learn more about the City’s commitment to &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.mississauga.ca/our-organization/equity-diversity-and-inclusion/&quot;&gt;Equity, Diversity and Inclusion&lt;/a&gt;. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Accommodations&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt; The City of Mississauga is an Equal Opportunity Employer and is committed to removing barriers in our selection process for people with visible and invisible disabilities. In accordance with the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act, 2005 and the Ontario Human Rights Code, the City of Mississauga will provide accommodations throughout the recruitment, selection and/or assessment process to applicants with disabilities. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt; If selected to participate in the recruitment, selection and/or assessment process, please complete the following &lt;a title=&quot;&quot; href=&quot;https://www7.mississauga.ca/documents/inside/talent/accommodation_request_form.pdf&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener&quot;&gt;Accommodation Request Form&lt;/a&gt; and have it emailed to &lt;a href=&quot;mailto:recruitment.accommodation@mississauga.ca&quot;&gt;recruitment.accommodation@mississauga.ca&lt;/a&gt; citing the Job ID and Job Title. This will inform Human Resources of the nature of any accommodation(s) that you may require in respect of any materials or processes used to ensure your equal participation. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0.0px;text-align:left&quot;&gt; &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0.0px;text-align:left&quot;&gt; &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://www7.mississauga.ca/documents/inside/talent/forbes_2026_footer_image.jpg&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; width=&quot;450&quot; height=&quot;101&quot;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:justify;margin:0.0&quot;&gt;Req ID: 28647&lt;br&gt;Vacancy Type: Permanent &lt;br&gt;Number of Positions: 1  &lt;br&gt;Closing Date: 10/16/2026&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;padding:10.0px 0.0px;border:1.0px solid transparent&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:18.0px;word-wrap:break-word&quot;&gt;&lt;H2 style=&quot;font-size:1.0em;margin:0.0px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Job Summary&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/H2&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;As the City of Mississauga intensifies, planning for, delivering parkland, and protecting City parkland assets becomes increasingly challenging and essential as we strive to create healthy complete communities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Parks Assets, Urban Design team consists of both planners and landscape architects who work together to plan parks, expand the City&apos;s parkland and greenlands, protect park assets; and comment on development applications, and City parkland matters.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Under the direction of the Lead Parkland Planner, the successful applicant will be responsible for representing the departmental interests on development applications and realty matters which include license/easement agreements, parkland acquisition, as well as parkland planning studies and other technical studies. This position will require the ability to resolve issues within a fast paced environment, manage several projects at one time, have a full breadth of knowledge of the planning process, comment on legal agreements, and have excellent public communication skills.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;padding:10.0px 0.0px;border:1.0px solid transparent&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:18.0px;word-wrap:break-word&quot;&gt;&lt;H2 style=&quot;font-size:1.0em;margin:0.0px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Duties and Responsibilities&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/H2&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Reporting to the Manager of Urban Design, the successful candidate will:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare, review and manage comments on all types of Development Applications, Environmental Assessments, Realty Requests and associated Agreements related to Parkland and Greenlands, including Parkland Cash-in-lieu determinations on behalf of Parks Assets, Urban Design&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordination, review, and preparation of comments related to license and easement agreements, land acquisition and surplus declarations that impact City owned parkland and greenland&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Liaises and meets with public agencies and departments, professionals, consultants, elected officials, staff, residents and special interest groups as required with respect to the projects and the future development of parks and recreational facilities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Attend and lead public meetings for presentation as well as provides professional advice and input to the public, Council and other professionals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Research and prepare reports to Committees and Council&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Attend and provide evidence at Ontario Land Tribunal hearings&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Performs other related duties as assigned&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;padding:10.0px 0.0px;border:1.0px solid transparent&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:18.0px;word-wrap:break-word&quot;&gt;&lt;H2 style=&quot;font-size:1.0em;margin:0.0px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Skills and Qualifications&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/H2&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Graduate from a recognized university in Planning or related discipline with a minimum of 5 years of experience in development planning&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated knowledge and experience of municipal land development processes including subdivision, rezoning and site plan applications as well as servicing and development agreements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to liaise with elected officials, other City Departments, federal &amp;amp; provincial authorities, conservation &amp;amp; regional authorities, and other outside agencies as required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated project management and time management skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent oral and written communication skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to provide detailed analysis of development applications and to negotiate and advocate for Parks Assets, Urban Design interests&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work well in a team environment and independently&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of related computer applications required including Microsoft Suite software and ePlans&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Eligibility for membership in the Ontario Professional Planners Institute and Canadian Institute of Planners is required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must have ability to travel to sites and provide own transportation and be comfortable working flexible hours&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0.0px;text-align:left&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt;Hourly Rate/Salary: $ 91,701.00 - $ 122,268.00&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt;Hours of Work: 35&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt;Work Location: Civic Centre&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;color:black&quot;&gt;Hybrid Workplace &lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt;Department/Division/Section: P&amp;amp;B/Planning &amp;amp; Building Dept , P&amp;amp;B/Develop &amp;amp; Design Division , Urban Design&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt;Non-Union/Union: Non Union&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0.0px;text-align:left&quot;&gt; &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0.0px;text-align:left&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt;The City of Mississauga may use artificial intelligence (AI) technology in sourcing and/or screening candidates for some positions; however, it is not used in selecting final candidates. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt; We thank all who apply, however, only those candidates selected for an interview will be contacted. You can also check your application status in your candidate profile online. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt; All personal information is collected under the authority of the Municipal Act. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equity, Diversity and Inclusion&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt; The City of Mississauga is committed to creating a respectful and supportive workplace that fosters a culture of equity, diversity and inclusion which broadly reflects the communities and residents we serve. Throughout the employee life cycle, the City is working to include an EDI lens to attract, retain and support the growth of diverse talent. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt; Learn more about the City’s commitment to &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.mississauga.ca/our-organization/equity-diversity-and-inclusion/&quot;&gt;Equity, Diversity and Inclusion&lt;/a&gt;. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Accommodations&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt; The City of Mississauga is an Equal Opportunity Employer and is committed to removing barriers in our selection process for people with visible and invisible disabilities. In accordance with the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act, 2005 and the Ontario Human Rights Code, the City of Mississauga will provide accommodations throughout the recruitment, selection and/or assessment process to applicants with disabilities. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt; If selected to participate in the recruitment, selection and/or assessment process, please complete the following &lt;a title=&quot;&quot; href=&quot;https://www7.mississauga.ca/documents/inside/talent/accommodation_request_form.pdf&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener&quot;&gt;Accommodation Request Form&lt;/a&gt; and have it emailed to &lt;a href=&quot;mailto:recruitment.accommodation@mississauga.ca&quot;&gt;recruitment.accommodation@mississauga.ca&lt;/a&gt; citing the Job ID and Job Title. This will inform Human Resources of the nature of any accommodation(s) that you may require in respect of any materials or processes used to ensure your equal participation. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0.0px;text-align:left&quot;&gt; &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0.0px;text-align:left&quot;&gt; &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://www7.mississauga.ca/documents/inside/talent/forbes_2026_footer_image.jpg&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; width=&quot;450&quot; height=&quot;101&quot;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:justify;margin:0.0&quot;&gt;Req ID: 28077&lt;br&gt;Vacancy Type: Permanent &lt;br&gt;Number of Positions: 13  &lt;br&gt;Closing Date: 11/16/2026&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;padding:10.0px 0.0px;border:1.0px solid transparent&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:18.0px;word-wrap:break-word&quot;&gt;&lt;H2 style=&quot;font-size:1.0em;margin:0.0px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Job Summary&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/H2&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:justify&quot;&gt; &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:justify&quot;&gt;Do you want to help move people across the city? Do you enjoy working in a fast-paced environment? MiWay is looking for enthusiastic individuals with a passion to perform quality mechanical and electrical repairs on transit buses and non-revenue fleet vehicle. If that’s you, then come on board! Help the public get where they need to be, by becoming a Transit Mechanic with MiWay.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:justify&quot;&gt; &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:justify&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why Work for MiWay?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Start with MiWay as a Full-Time Permanent;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Career advancement opportunities;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive compensation and benefits package with pension (OMERS Retirement Savings Plan);
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Starting Rate: $50.53 Per hour + Additional pay:
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sunday Shift Premium - time and one-half (1½) the regular hourly rate&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Afternoons Shift Premium - $1/hour&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Night Shift Premium - $2/hour&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tool Allowance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;And much more..&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;padding:10.0px 0.0px;border:1.0px solid transparent&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:18.0px;word-wrap:break-word&quot;&gt;&lt;H2 style=&quot;font-size:1.0em;margin:0.0px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Duties and Responsibilities&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/H2&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;color:black&quot;&gt; &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;color:black&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:black&quot;&gt;Perform maintenance and repairs to the MiWay Transit Fleet as set forth by the policy of the Fleet Maintenance Section.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;color:black&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:black&quot;&gt;Must be able to read and understand various schematics related to MiWay Transit Fleet vehicles.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;color:black&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:black&quot;&gt;Use laptop computers to diagnose electrical and electronic system faults.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;color:black&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:black&quot;&gt;Must be proficient in the use of electronic diagnostic readers.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;color:black&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:black&quot;&gt;Must be able to meet reasonable time expectancy in performing assigned duties.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;color:black&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:black&quot;&gt;Work on Transit Fleet vehicles under inclement weather conditions.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;color:black&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:black&quot;&gt;Undertake road call diagnosis and repair.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;color:black&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:black&quot;&gt;Must wear the appropriate Personal Protective Equipment (PPE).&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:black&quot;&gt;Must posses own green patch CSA approved safety footwear.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;color:black&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:black&quot;&gt;Must posses all necessary hand tools used to perform inspections, services and repairs.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;color:black&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:black&quot;&gt;Perform other related duties as assigned.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;padding:10.0px 0.0px;border:1.0px solid transparent&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:18.0px;word-wrap:break-word&quot;&gt;&lt;H2 style=&quot;font-size:1.0em;margin:0.0px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Skills and Qualifications&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/H2&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Minimum grade 12 - Ontario Secondary School Diploma (OSSD) or verified equivalent, is considered an asset.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Valid 310T - Truck and Coach Technician Certificate of Qualification, issued by Skilled Trades Ontario and maintained in good standing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;310S – Automotive Service Technician trade licence is an asset.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A minimum of five (5) years of combined experience as an Apperentice and Journeyperson.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must have a valid G Driver’s License; D or C Ontario Driver’s License with a “Z” endorsement is preferred. A driver’s license abstract acceptable to the CIty is also required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with electronic multiplexed Heavy Duty diesel engine and automatic transmission vehicles is preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Additional courses in the mechanic’s trade will be an asset.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with computerized work orders preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of the O.H. &amp;amp; S. Act and Regulations, including WHMIS, and the Ministry of Transportation Highway Traffic Act is preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work independently with minimum supervision.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability and willingness to stay current with new technologies and equipment to perform bus repairs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working experience in a Unionized environment is an asset.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0.0px;text-align:left&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt;Hourly Rate/Salary: $50.53&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt;Hours of Work: 40&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt;Work Location: Mississauga Transit&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt;Department/Division/Section: T&amp;amp;W/Transportation&amp;amp;Works Dept , T&amp;amp;W/Mississauga Transit , MT Maintenance&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt;Non-Union/Union: Transit&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0.0px;text-align:left&quot;&gt; &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0.0px;text-align:left&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt; The City of Mississauga may use artificial intelligence (AI) technology in sourcing candidates for some positions, however, it is not being used for screening, assessing, or selecting candidates. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt; We thank all who apply, however, only those candidates selected for an interview will be contacted. You can also check your application status in your candidate profile online. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt; All personal information is collected under the authority of the Municipal Act. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equity, Diversity and Inclusion&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt; The City of Mississauga is committed to creating a respectful and supportive workplace that fosters a culture of equity, diversity and inclusion which broadly reflects the communities and residents we serve. Throughout the employee life cycle, the City is working to include an EDI lens to attract, retain and support the growth of diverse talent. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt; Learn more about the City’s commitment to &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.mississauga.ca/our-organization/equity-diversity-and-inclusion/&quot;&gt;Equity, Diversity and Inclusion&lt;/a&gt;. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Accommodations&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt; The City of Mississauga is an Equal Opportunity Employer and is committed to removing barriers in our selection process for people with visible and invisible disabilities. In accordance with the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act, 2005 and the Ontario Human Rights Code, the City of Mississauga will provide accommodations throughout the recruitment, selection and/or assessment process to applicants with disabilities. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt; If selected to participate in the recruitment, selection and/or assessment process, please complete the following &lt;a title=&quot;&quot; href=&quot;https://www7.mississauga.ca/documents/inside/talent/accommodation_request_form.pdf&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener&quot;&gt;Accommodation Request Form&lt;/a&gt; and have it emailed to &lt;a href=&quot;mailto:recruitment.accommodation@mississauga.ca&quot;&gt;recruitment.accommodation@mississauga.ca&lt;/a&gt; citing the Job ID and Job Title. This will inform Human Resources of the nature of any accommodation(s) that you may require in respect of any materials or processes used to ensure your equal participation. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0.0px;text-align:left&quot;&gt; &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0.0px;text-align:left&quot;&gt; &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://www7.mississauga.ca/documents/inside/talent/forbes_2026_footer_image.jpg&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; width=&quot;450&quot; height=&quot;101&quot;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:justify;margin:0.0&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt;Req ID: 28471&lt;br&gt;Vacancy Type: Permanent &lt;br&gt;Number of Positions: 3  &lt;br&gt;Closing Date: 11/16/2026&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;padding:10.0px 0.0px;border:1.0px solid transparent&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:18.0px;word-wrap:break-word&quot;&gt;&lt;H2 style=&quot;font-size:1.0em;margin:0.0px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Job Summary&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/H2&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;MiWay is seeking experienced and motivated leaders to supervise the day-to-day maintenance of transit buses and non revenue fleet vehicles.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Reporting to the Assistant Manager, Transit Maintenance, the Supervisor is responsible for leading skilled trades staff in a unionized, safety critical environment to ensure vehicles are safe, compliant, and ready for service. This position plays a key role in supporting daily service delivery, fleet availability, and MiWay’s commitment to safety, reliability, and customer service. &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;Guided by a forward thinking strategic plan, MiWay’s vision is to be a transit system that makes Mississauga proud by providing a safe, reliable, and efficient transit system built on strong traditions of safety, service, and courtesy. &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why Work for MiWay&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Full time, permanent employment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive salary&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Annual performance and economic adjustment reviews&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Career advancement opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Four (4) weeks of paid vacation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comprehensive benefits package&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;OMERS pension plan&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Overtime premiums&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Skilled trades premiums - $1.75/hour&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Afternoon shift premiums - $2.00/hour&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Overnight shift premiums - $2.75/hour&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;And more.&lt;br&gt; &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Note&lt;/strong&gt;: This position requires a valid 310T Truck and Coach certificate and flexibility to work different hours, shifts, and days off to be considered.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;padding:10.0px 0.0px;border:1.0px solid transparent&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:18.0px;word-wrap:break-word&quot;&gt;&lt;H2 style=&quot;font-size:1.0em;margin:0.0px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Duties and Responsibilities&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/H2&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Under the direction of the Assistant Manager, Transit Maintenance, the successful candidate will:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Supervise the day to day activities of Transit Maintenance staff to ensure the safe, efficient, and timely inspection, repair, cleaning, and servicing of transit buses and non revenue fleet vehicles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assign work, allocate personnel and equipment, and adjust priorities to support daily fleet availability and service requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Schedule maintenance activities and prepare work orders using a computerized maintenance management system.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure all maintenance work complies with Ministry of Transportation legislation, applicable safety regulations, manufacturer specifications, and MiWay policies and procedures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide front line leadership by setting clear performance expectations, monitoring work quality, and supporting staff through coaching and feedback.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage staffing requirements, attendance, overtime, and shift coverage in accordance with operational needs and collective agreements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work collaboratively with management, Human Resources, and union representatives to address employee relations matters and support effective labour relations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Respond to service impacting failures, road calls, incidents, and urgent maintenance issues as required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure staff are properly instructed in safe work practices, approved methods, procedures, and performance standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the onboarding, orientation, and ongoing development of MiWay  Maintenance staff.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support and, when required, supervise the operation of bus wash area, fueling stations, and bus cleaning activities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor and manage records including absences, overtime, incident reports, and operational data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist with identifying warranty issues, tagging defective components, and ensuring warranty claims and supplier commitments are upheld.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure tools, parts, materials, and cores are properly handled, stored, returned, or disposed of in accordance with procedures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct technical investigations, inspections, and procedural or quality audits as required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Promote a safe, respectful, and inclusive workplace that is free from harassment and discrimination.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support MiWay’s commitments under the Ontario Human Rights Code (OHRC), the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act, and related corporate policies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform other related duties as assigned.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;padding:10.0px 0.0px;border:1.0px solid transparent&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:18.0px;word-wrap:break-word&quot;&gt;&lt;H2 style=&quot;font-size:1.0em;margin:0.0px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Skills and Qualifications&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/H2&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Minimum grade 12 - Ontario Secondary School Diploma (OSSD) or verified equivalent, is considered an asset.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Valid 310T - Truck and Coach Technician Certificate of Qualification, issued by Skilled Trades Ontario and maintained in good standing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A minimum of five (5) years of experience as a Journeyperson following attainment of trade certification, with exposure to the full range of transit bus maintenance activities or an equivalent combination of education / certifications and experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Three (3) years of progressive experience demonstrating leadership responsibility, including supervision or acting supervisory duties is preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A valid 310S Automotive Service Technician Certificate of Qualification, issued by Skilled Trades Ontario, is considered an asset.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Valid Ontario Class G Driver’s Licence with an acceptable driving abstract; a Class C licence with Z endorsement is preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work various shifts including days, afternoons, nights, weekends, and statutory holidays.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong working knowledge of heavy vehicle maintenance, diagnostics, and manufacturer specifications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of shop management practices, preventative maintenance programs, and applicable OHSA, MTO, MOL, and MOE legislative requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to lead, coach, and support employees in a unionized environment, with a focus on safety, collaboration, consistency, and respectful workplace practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong interpersonal, organizational, and written and verbal communication skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience or exposure to battery electric buses or alternative propulsion technologies is considered an asset.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0.0px;text-align:left&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt;Hourly Rate/Salary: $91,701.00 - $122,268.00&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt;Hours of Work: 40&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt;Work Location: Mississauga Transit&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt;Department/Division/Section: T&amp;amp;W/Transportation&amp;amp;Works Dept , T&amp;amp;W/Mississauga Transit , MT Maintenance&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt;Non-Union/Union: Non Union&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0.0px;text-align:left&quot;&gt; &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0.0px;text-align:left&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt;The City of Mississauga may use artificial intelligence (AI) technology in sourcing and/or screening candidates for some positions; however, it is not used in selecting final candidates. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt; We thank all who apply, however, only those candidates selected for an interview will be contacted. You can also check your application status in your candidate profile online. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt; All personal information is collected under the authority of the Municipal Act. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equity, Diversity and Inclusion&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt; The City of Mississauga is committed to creating a respectful and supportive workplace that fosters a culture of equity, diversity and inclusion which broadly reflects the communities and residents we serve. Throughout the employee life cycle, the City is working to include an EDI lens to attract, retain and support the growth of diverse talent. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt; Learn more about the City’s commitment to &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.mississauga.ca/our-organization/equity-diversity-and-inclusion/&quot;&gt;Equity, Diversity and Inclusion&lt;/a&gt;. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Accommodations&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt; The City of Mississauga is an Equal Opportunity Employer and is committed to removing barriers in our selection process for people with visible and invisible disabilities. In accordance with the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act, 2005 and the Ontario Human Rights Code, the City of Mississauga will provide accommodations throughout the recruitment, selection and/or assessment process to applicants with disabilities. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt; If selected to participate in the recruitment, selection and/or assessment process, please complete the following &lt;a title=&quot;&quot; href=&quot;https://www7.mississauga.ca/documents/inside/talent/accommodation_request_form.pdf&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener&quot;&gt;Accommodation Request Form&lt;/a&gt; and have it emailed to &lt;a href=&quot;mailto:recruitment.accommodation@mississauga.ca&quot;&gt;recruitment.accommodation@mississauga.ca&lt;/a&gt; citing the Job ID and Job Title. This will inform Human Resources of the nature of any accommodation(s) that you may require in respect of any materials or processes used to ensure your equal participation. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0.0px;text-align:left&quot;&gt; &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0.0px;text-align:left&quot;&gt; &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://www7.mississauga.ca/documents/inside/talent/forbes_2026_footer_image.jpg&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; width=&quot;450&quot; height=&quot;101&quot;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:justify;margin:0.0&quot;&gt;Req ID: 28646&lt;br&gt;Vacancy Type: Permanent &lt;br&gt;Number of Positions: 1  &lt;br&gt;Closing Date: 10/16/2026&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;padding:10.0px 0.0px;border:1.0px solid transparent&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:18.0px;word-wrap:break-word&quot;&gt;&lt;H2 style=&quot;font-size:1.0em;margin:0.0px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Job Summary&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/H2&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:10.0pt;color:black&quot;&gt;Reporting to the Supervisor of Operations and working in collaboration with the facility team, the Facility Operator I will provide operational facility cleaning, general maintenance and repair services to facilities while providing excellent customer service. As well, supports the Supervisor of Operations in coordinating and overseeing the work of Facility Operators plus additional administrative duties.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;padding:10.0px 0.0px;border:1.0px solid transparent&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:18.0px;word-wrap:break-word&quot;&gt;&lt;H2 style=&quot;font-size:1.0em;margin:0.0px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Duties and Responsibilities&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/H2&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:10.0pt;color:black&quot;&gt;Assist the Supervisor of Operations in developing and monitoring the annual work plan for operations and future capital projects and lead facility projects including but not limited to ice installation &amp;amp; removal, pool shutdowns and pool start-ups &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:10.0pt;color:black&quot;&gt;Collaborate with a team of facility operators performing facility maintenance duties including general cleaning, refinishing floors, room set-ups and waste collection &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:10.0pt;color:black&quot;&gt;Create duties and train part-time operations staff and volunteer workers&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:10.0pt;color:black&quot;&gt;Generate and assign preventative maintenance work orders on various mechanical systems including HVAC, boilers, pool filtration and arena refrigeration equipment&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:10.0pt;color:black&quot;&gt;Maintain ice surface(s), perform plant readings, use and maintain ice resurfacer machine, pool filtration systems, water chemistry tests, adding chemicals and pool troubleshooting&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:10.0pt;color:black&quot;&gt;Organize and lead minor maintenance repairs such as but not limited to plumbing, electrical and carpentry  &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:10.0pt;color:black&quot;&gt;Support the Supervisor of Operations with flagging and reporting any major repairs that require a higher level of service or tradesperson or external vendor&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:10.0pt;color:black&quot;&gt;Other duties assigned&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;padding:10.0px 0.0px;border:1.0px solid transparent&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:18.0px;word-wrap:break-word&quot;&gt;&lt;H2 style=&quot;font-size:1.0em;margin:0.0px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Skills and Qualifications&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/H2&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:10.0pt;color:black&quot;&gt;Secondary School diploma with experience working as a Facility Operator, including experience providing technical and hands-on expertise in arenas and pools, and experience planning facility projects and completing them on time&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:10.0pt;color:black&quot;&gt;Ability to operate an ice resurfacer, edger and various power and hand tools required&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:10.0pt;color:black&quot;&gt;Ability to prioritize, multitask and work to complete deadlines in a fast paced environment&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:10.0pt;color:black&quot;&gt;CIT (Certified Ice Technician) certification including Ice Making and Equipment Operation, Ice Making and Painting Technologies and Legal Awareness I is considered an asset&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:10.0pt;color:black&quot;&gt; and possession of a “B” (Refrigeration Operator Class B) ticket is required to work at “registered plant facilities” deemed by the Province of Ontario. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:10.0pt;color:black&quot;&gt;Current CPO (Certified Pool Operator) certification required&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:10.0pt;color:black&quot;&gt;Knowledgeable in working with Microsoft Office (Outlook, Word, Excel), Building Automation Systems (BAS) and Work Order Systems (Work and Service Order Requests)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:10.0pt;color:black&quot;&gt;Must be physically capable of carrying out the essential duties of the job&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:10.0pt;color:black&quot;&gt;Must hold and provide a copy of a valid Ontario Driver’s License Class G&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:10.0pt;color:black&quot;&gt;Professional experience in custodial/janitorial work and facility maintenance&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:10.0pt;color:black&quot;&gt; Valid CPR, First Aid Certification or willing to obtain in the first six months of employment&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0.0px;text-align:left&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:10.0pt;color:black&quot;&gt;Hourly Rate/Salary: $ 70,807.00 - $ 94,410.00 &lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:10.0pt;color:black&quot;&gt;Grade: D &lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:10.0pt;color:black&quot;&gt;Hours of Work: 40 hours per week &lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:10.0pt;color:black&quot;&gt;Department/Division/Section: CMS/Community Services Dept , CMS/Recreation &amp;amp; Culture Division  &lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:10.0pt;color:black&quot;&gt;Non-Union/Union: Non Union &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0.0px;text-align:left&quot;&gt; &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0.0px;text-align:left&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:10.0pt;color:black&quot;&gt;The City of Mississauga may use artificial intelligence (AI) technology in sourcing and/or screening candidates for some positions; however, it is not used in selecting final candidates. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:left&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:10.0pt;color:black&quot;&gt; Applicants applying to this posting may be considered for the same position(s) should another vacancy occur within six months from the date of this posting, unless the requirement to repost is expressed differently in a Collective Agreement. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:10.0pt;color:black&quot;&gt; If you are selected for an interview and your proposed transfer or promotion results in a real or perceived conflict of interest in relation to the Employment of Relatives Corporate Policy and Procedure, you must notify the Human Resources Representative as soon as possible. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:10.0pt;color:black&quot;&gt; If you are selected for an interview you are expected to disclose all current positions held in the City, whether full time or part time. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:left&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:10.0pt;color:black&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equity, Diversity and Inclusion&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:10.0pt;color:black&quot;&gt; The City of Mississauga is committed to creating a respectful and supportive workplace that fosters a culture of equity, diversity and inclusion which broadly reflects the communities and residents we serve. Throughout the employee life cycle, the City is working to include an EDI lens to attract, retain and support the growth of diverse talent. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:10.0pt;color:black&quot;&gt; Learn more about the City’s commitment to &lt;a style=&quot;color:black&quot; href=&quot;https://www.mississauga.ca/our-organization/equity-diversity-and-inclusion/&quot;&gt;Equity, Diversity and Inclusion&lt;/a&gt;. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:10.0pt;color:black&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Accommodations&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:10.0pt;color:black&quot;&gt; The City of Mississauga is an Equal Opportunity Employer and is committed to removing barriers in our selection process for people with visible and invisible disabilities. In accordance with the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act, 2005 and the Ontario Human Rights Code, the City of Mississauga will provide accommodations throughout the recruitment, selection and/or assessment process to applicants with disabilities. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:10.0pt;color:black&quot;&gt; If selected to participate in the recruitment, selection and/or assessment process, please complete the following &lt;a style=&quot;color:black&quot; title=&quot;&quot; href=&quot;https://www7.mississauga.ca/documents/inside/talent/accommodation_request_form.pdf&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener&quot;&gt;Accommodation Request Form&lt;/a&gt; and have it emailed to &lt;a style=&quot;color:black&quot; href=&quot;mailto:recruitment.accommodation@mississauga.ca&quot;&gt;recruitment.accommodation@mississauga.ca&lt;/a&gt; citing the Job ID and Job Title. This will inform Human Resources of the nature of any accommodation(s) that you may require in respect of any materials or processes used to ensure your equal participation. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:left&quot;&gt; &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:left&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:10.0pt;color:black&quot;&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://www7.mississauga.ca/documents/inside/talent/forbes_2026_footer_image.jpg&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; width=&quot;450&quot; height=&quot;101&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:justify&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt;Req ID: 28684 &lt;br&gt;Vacancy Type: Temporary &lt;br&gt;Contract Duration: January - April, 2027&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt;Number of Positions: 1  &lt;br&gt;Closing Date: 10/22/2026&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:justify&quot;&gt; &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:justify&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;To be considered for this competition, applicants must be enrolled in a recognized post‑secondary co-op program and be eligible to complete a Work Term during the specified period. Applicants must be legally eligible to work in Canada. Proof of enrolment in a related program must be uploaded when completing the application.&lt;/strong&gt;   &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;padding:10.0px 0.0px;border:1.0px solid transparent&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:18.0px;word-wrap:break-word&quot;&gt;&lt;H2 style=&quot;font-size:1.0em;margin:0.0px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Job Summary&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/H2&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;The City of Mississauga is seeking a motivated individual who is looking to make a positive impact and will be responsible for assisting the Energy Management team with the day-to-day duties. The successful candidate will be part of a team of engaged, enthusiastic and dedicated people that are committed to collaborating with one another to deliver on our commitment to the residents, visitors and businesses of Mississauga.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;padding:10.0px 0.0px;border:1.0px solid transparent&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:18.0px;word-wrap:break-word&quot;&gt;&lt;H2 style=&quot;font-size:1.0em;margin:0.0px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Duties and Responsibilities&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/H2&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Under the guidance of the Energy Management team, the successful candidate will be required to support the Energy Management and Facility Maintenance sections in various projects and initiatives. Responsibilities include:&lt;br&gt;•    Assist with utilities management&lt;br&gt;•    Assist with Energy Benchmarking and Re-commissioning&lt;br&gt;•    Analyse data and provide support with reporting&lt;br&gt;•    Assist with database management (data entry and validation)&lt;br&gt;•    Collect and verify site equipment data for HVAC, lighting, water fixtures, refrigeration and other mechanical, electrical equipment/systems through site visits and documented information&lt;br&gt;•    Assist in estimating energy consumption of new City facilities for financial utility budgets&lt;br&gt;•    Assist in monitoring Building Automation Systems and live metering system for abnormalities in energy consumption&lt;br&gt;•    Assist in configuring and managing the Energy Management Information Software (SkySpark)&lt;br&gt;•    Assist in preparing grant applications for various incentive programs&lt;br&gt;•    Assist with maintenance contracts management&lt;br&gt;•    Assist with data analysis and Power BI reports creation&lt;br&gt;•    Assist with maintenance of the CMMS (Computerized Maintenance Management System) for building assets&lt;br&gt;•    Assist with testing and troubleshooting&lt;br&gt;•    Assist with Asset inventory&lt;br&gt;•    Perform other duties as required&lt;br&gt;•    Duties and responsibilities may vary according to the student&apos;s academic background and experience.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;padding:10.0px 0.0px;border:1.0px solid transparent&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:18.0px;word-wrap:break-word&quot;&gt;&lt;H2 style=&quot;font-size:1.0em;margin:0.0px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Skills and Qualifications&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/H2&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;•    Currently enrolled in a program of study in Electrical Engineering, Mechanical/Mechatronics Engineering, Management Science, Environmental studies, Systems Design Engineering or related discipline at a recognized university in a co-op program;&lt;br&gt;•    High level of enthusiasm as well as strong verbal and written communication skills are required;&lt;br&gt;•    Strong interpersonal skills and ability to collaborate with other teams;&lt;br&gt;•    Proficiency in computer programing languages (e.g. VBA, Python, SQL,etc.) is preferred;&lt;br&gt;•    Strong analytical skills;&lt;br&gt;•    Experience with database management is an asset;&lt;br&gt;•    Demonstrated ability to plan and organize work;&lt;br&gt;•    Solid proficiency in Excel, Word, and other MS Office programs is required; and,&lt;br&gt;•    Exceptional customer service skills&lt;br&gt;•    The successful candidate must be willing and able to travel to various locations as required, with responsibility for arranging their own transportation&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:left&quot;&gt;Hourly Rate/Salary: 20.64 - 24.53&lt;br&gt;Hours of Work: 35&lt;br&gt;Work Location: Civic Centre&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:black&quot;&gt;Hybrid Workplace &lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;Organization Unit: CMS/Energy Management&lt;br&gt;Department/Division/Section: CMS/Community Services Dept , CMS/Facilities &amp;amp; Property Management , Energy Management&lt;br&gt;Non-Union/Union: Non Union&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Applicants applying to this posting may be considered for the same position(s) should another vacancy occur within six months from the date of this posting, unless the requirement to repost is expressed differently in a Collective Agreement.&lt;br&gt;If you are selected for an interview and your proposed transfer or promotion results in a real or perceived conflict of interest in relation to the Employment of Relatives Corporate Policy and Procedure, you must notify the Human Resources Representative as soon as possible.&lt;br&gt;If you are selected for an interview you are expected to disclose all current positions held in the City, whether full time or part time.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI (Artificial Intelligence)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The City of Mississauga may use artificial intelligence (AI) technology in sourcing and/or screening candidates for some positions; however, it is not used in selecting final candidates&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Candidates are expected to complete interviews independently to ensure an equitable assessment. The use of AI-generated responses, AI assistants, transcription tools, or third-party coaching technologies during interviews is prohibited, unless supported by an approved accommodation and may result in disqualification from the recruitment process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Accommodations&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;The City of Mississauga is an Equal Opportunity Employer and is committed to removing barriers in our selection process for people with visible and invisible disabilities. In accordance with the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act, 2005 and the Ontario Human Rights Code, the City of Mississauga will provide accommodations throughout the recruitment, selection and/or assessment process to applicants with disabilities.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;If selected to participate in the recruitment, selection and/or assessment process, please complete the following &lt;a href=&quot;https://www7.mississauga.ca/documents/inside/talent/accommodation_request_form.pdf&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener&quot;&gt;Accommodation Request Form&lt;/a&gt; and have it emailed to &lt;a href=&quot;mailto:recruitment.accommodation@mississauga.ca&quot;&gt;recruitment.accommodation@mississauga.ca&lt;/a&gt; citing the Job ID and Job Title. This will inform Human Resources of the nature of any accommodation(s) that you may require in respect of any materials or processes used to ensure your equal participation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0.0px;text-align:left&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equity, Diversity and Inclusion&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;The City of Mississauga is committed to creating a respectful and supportive workplace that fosters a culture of equity, diversity and inclusion which broadly reflects the communities and residents we serve. Throughout the employee life cycle, the City is working to include an EDI lens to attract, retain and support the growth of diverse talent.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Learn more about the City’s commitment to &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.mississauga.ca/our-organization/equity-diversity-and-inclusion/&quot;&gt;Equity, Diversity and Inclusion&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:left&quot;&gt; &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:left&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt; &lt;img src=&quot;https://www7.mississauga.ca/documents/inside/talent/forbes_2026_footer_image.jpg&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; width=&quot;450&quot; height=&quot;101&quot;&gt; &lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:justify;margin:0.0&quot;&gt;Req ID: 28690&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:justify;margin:0.0&quot;&gt;Number of Positions: 2 &lt;br&gt;Vacancy Type: Combination  - 1 Permanent Position &amp;amp; 1 Temporary Position&lt;br&gt;Duration of Contract for Temporary Position: Up to 2 years&lt;br&gt;Closing Date: 10/30/2026&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;padding:10.0px 0.0px;border:1.0px solid transparent&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:18.0px;word-wrap:break-word&quot;&gt;&lt;H2 style=&quot;font-size:1.0em;margin:0.0px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Job Summary&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/H2&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Under the direction of Managers, Rapid Transit Program Office (RTPO), RTPO is seeking two experienced, motivated, and detail-oriented professionals to fill the role of PUCC/Permit Technologist.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The PUCC/Permit Technologist role will be responsible for conducting both office-based and field reviews of Public Utilities Coordinating Committee (PUCC) and Road Occupancy Permit (ROP) applications on behalf of the RTPO. This role supports the delivery of the City&apos;s major rapid transit initiatives, including the Eglinton Crosstown West Extension (ECWE), Bus Rapid Transit (BRT), and Hazel McCallion Light Rail Transit (HMLRT) projects.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Key responsibilities include ensuring compliance with City policies, procedures, standards, and applicable legislation; reviewing and evaluating new and existing permit applications; coordinating with internal and external stakeholders; and conducting site inspections to verify that work has been completed in accordance with approved permits and City requirements. The successful candidate will assess permit submissions, review supporting documentation, and perform field investigations as required to determine whether applications should be approved, modified, or returned for revision. Through these activities, the PUCC/Permit Technologist will play a critical role in supporting the safe, efficient, and coordinated delivery of municipal infrastructure and rapid transit projects across the city.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;padding:10.0px 0.0px;border:1.0px solid transparent&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:18.0px;word-wrap:break-word&quot;&gt;&lt;H2 style=&quot;font-size:1.0em;margin:0.0px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Duties and Responsibilities&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/H2&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reviews and evaluates Public Utilities Coordinating Committee (PUCC) and Road Occupancy Permit (ROP) applications in support of RTPO projects, in coordination and consultation with the City&apos;s Permitting and Technical Services sections, as required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensures compliance with City policies, procedures, standards, applicable legislation, and service timelines; maintains accurate electronic permit records and databases.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinates application reviews with internal departments, utility companies, contractors, consultants, and other project stakeholders; attends pre-construction meetings as required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinates meetings with utility companies and inspection staff to resolve conflicts between proposed or approved utility alignments and field conditions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provides technical guidance and support to staff, internal stakeholders, utility companies, contractors, and external applicants regarding utility applications and ROP requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conducts site visits, as required, to support the review and assessment of proposed PUCC and ROP applications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Performs site inspections to verify compliance with permit conditions and confirm completion of approved works in accordance with City by-laws, standards, and municipal requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identifies, assesses, and helps resolve permit-related issues, conflicts, and operational impacts affecting rapid transit infrastructure and projects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reviews permit submissions and provides recommendations regarding approval, revision, or rejection based on applicable requirements and site conditions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintains accurate records, correspondence, reports, and supporting documentation related to permit reviews and inspections.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensures the timely investigation, response, and resolution of inquiries, complaints, and service requests received from residents, elected officials, and other stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conducts research and assists in the development of programs, initiatives, policies, and strategies that support RTPO objectives and the City of Mississauga&apos;s strategic priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the successful delivery of the ECWE, BRT, and HMLRT programs through effective permit administration, stakeholder coordination, and field oversight.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepares reports, correspondence, and briefing materials related to permit matters, as required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Performs other related duties as assigned.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;padding:10.0px 0.0px;border:1.0px solid transparent&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:18.0px;word-wrap:break-word&quot;&gt;&lt;H2 style=&quot;font-size:1.0em;margin:0.0px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Skills and Qualifications&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/H2&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Successful completion of a diploma in Civil Engineering Technology from a recognized Community College / University Degree with a minimum of 2 years of progressive experience in permitting, construction and maintenance of services infrastructure (or an equivalent combination of education and experience).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Membership in the Ontario Association of Certified Engineering Technicians and Technologists as a Certified Engineering Technologist (C.E.T.) or an equivalent designation considered an asset.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to co-ordinate complex utility or construction projects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of applicable legislative requirements such as the Occupational Health &amp;amp; Safety Act and Employment Standards Act.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong understanding of road maintenance procedures, Ontario Provincial Standards and Specifications (OPSS), utility infrastructure alignments and construction methodologies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must be able to read and interpret all types of engineering drawings, specifications and construction standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong interpersonal, communication and leadership skills are required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent organizational, computer skills and problem-solving abilities are required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must be able to multitask, function well in a team environment, and demonstrate a proven ability to work with a broad range of stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Computer literacy in CAD and Microsoft applications including Access.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with GIS programs, INFOR Public Sector Application Software and SAP is an asset.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to travel to various work locations as and when required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0.0px;text-align:left&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt;Hourly Rate/Salary: $ 44.27 - $59.03 / $ 80,567.00 - $ 107,426.00&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt;Hours of Work: 35&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt;Work Location: Rapid Transit Program Office - This role follows a hybrid work model, requiring employees to be onsite in the office 3 days per week. Specific in-office days may be set by the team or department to support collaboration and business needs.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt;Department/Division/Section: T&amp;amp;W/Transportation&amp;amp;Works Dept , T&amp;amp;W/Rapid Transit Program Office , Rapid Transit - Third Party&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif&quot;&gt;Non-Union/Union: Non Union&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0.0px;text-align:left&quot;&gt; &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We thank all who apply, however, only those candidates selected for an interview will be contacted. You can also check your application status in your candidate profile online.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;All personal information is collected under the authority of the Municipal Act. &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI (Artificial Intelligence)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The City of Mississauga may use artificial intelligence (AI) technology in sourcing and/or screening candidates for some positions; however, it is not used in selecting final candidates&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Candidates are expected to complete interviews independently to ensure an equitable assessment. The use of AI-generated responses, AI assistants, transcription tools, or third-party coaching technologies during interviews is prohibited, unless supported by an approved accommodation and may result in disqualification from the recruitment process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Accommodations&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;The City of Mississauga is an Equal Opportunity Employer and is committed to removing barriers in our selection process for people with visible and invisible disabilities. In accordance with the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act, 2005 and the Ontario Human Rights Code, the City of Mississauga will provide accommodations throughout the recruitment, selection and/or assessment process to applicants with disabilities.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;If selected to participate in the recruitment, selection and/or assessment process, please complete the following &lt;a href=&quot;https://www7.mississauga.ca/documents/inside/talent/accommodation_request_form.pdf&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener&quot;&gt;Accommodation Request Form&lt;/a&gt; and have it emailed to &lt;a href=&quot;mailto:recruitment.accommodation@mississauga.ca&quot;&gt;recruitment.accommodation@mississauga.ca&lt;/a&gt; citing the Job ID and Job Title. This will inform Human Resources of the nature of any accommodation(s) that you may require in respect of any materials or processes used to ensure your equal participation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0.0px;text-align:left&quot;&gt; &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0.0px;text-align:left&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equity, Diversity and Inclusion&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;The City of Mississauga is committed to creating a respectful and supportive workplace that fosters a culture of equity, diversity and inclusion which broadly reflects the communities and residents we serve. Throughout the employee life cycle, the City is working to include an EDI lens to attract, retain and support the growth of diverse talent.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Learn more about the City’s commitment to &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.mississauga.ca/our-organization/equity-diversity-and-inclusion/&quot;&gt;Equity, Diversity and Inclusion&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0.0px;text-align:left&quot;&gt; &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0.0px;text-align:left&quot;&gt; &lt;/p&gt;
